var e={"if too many buckets are in use:":`如果 被佔用的桶太多:`,"store key at bucket[hash(key) mod size]":`把 key 存到 bucket[hash(key) mod size]`,"make a table twice the size":`新建一張兩倍大的表`,"for each key in the old table:":`對每個 舊錶中的鍵:`,"put it at its bucket in the new one    // a different bucket":`把它放到新表中它的桶裡    // 一個不同的桶`,"let the old table go":`釋放舊錶`,"How full":`有多滿`,"A table filling up":`一張正在變滿的表`,"The table in front has four buckets and three keys: cat in 0, fox in 1, dog in 2. It is three-quarters full.":`前面這張表有四個桶和三個鍵：cat 在 0，fox 在 1，dog 在 2。它已經四分之三滿了。`,"How full a table is, keys divided by buckets, is its <strong>load factor</strong>. The row behind is a table twice the size, not yet in use.":`一張表有多滿，即鍵數除以桶數，叫作它的<strong>負載因子</strong>。後面那一排是一張兩倍大的表，還沒有使用。`,"Buckets in use":`被佔用的桶`,"Load factor":`負載因子`,"Collisions get likelier":`衝突越來越可能`,"Store bee. Its letters add up to 300, and 300 mod 4 is 0: where cat already is.":`存入 bee。它的字母加起來是 300，300 mod 4 是 0：cat 已經在那裡了。`,"With three of four buckets taken, a new key has a three-in-four chance of colliding. Chains lengthen, probes wander, and lookups stop being O(1).":`四個桶佔了三個，新鍵有四分之三的機率發生衝突。鏈變長，探測走得更遠，查詢也不再是 O(1)。`,"bee wants bucket 0 too":`bee 也想要 0 號桶`,"Past about 0.7 it is time to grow.":`超過大約 0.7，就該擴容了。`,"Move to a bigger table":`搬到更大的表`,Rehash:`再雜湊`,"So the table grows: twice the buckets. But the keys cannot just be copied across. A key’s bucket depends on the table size, so every one has to be <strong>rehashed</strong>.":`所以表擴容了：桶數翻倍。但鍵不能直接複製過去。鍵的桶取決於表的大小，所以每個鍵都必須<strong>重新雜湊</strong>。`,"cat: 312 mod 8 = 0. fox: 333 mod 8 = 5. dog: 314 mod 8 = 2. fox has moved from bucket 1 to bucket 5.":`cat：312 mod 8 = 0。fox：333 mod 8 = 5。dog：314 mod 8 = 2。fox 從 1 號桶搬到了 5 號桶。`,"Room again":`又有空間了`,"Now bee: 300 mod 8 = 4. Bucket 4 is free. The collision has gone, because the same keys are spread over twice as many buckets.":`現在是 bee：300 mod 8 = 4。4 號桶是空的。衝突消失了，因為同樣的鍵分佈在了兩倍多的桶裡。`,"Expensive, but rare":`昂貴，但少見`,"A resize touches every key, so that one insert costs O(n). But the table doubles each time, so resizes come twice as far apart as the table grows.":`一次擴容要處理每個鍵，所以那一次插入的代價是 O(n)。但表每次都翻倍，所以隨著表變大，擴容之間的間隔也會翻倍。`,"Spread over all the inserts, the extra work averages out to a constant: the insert is O(1) <strong>amortized</strong>. It is the same argument as for a dynamic array.":`分攤到所有插入上，額外的工作平均下來是一個常數：插入的<strong>均攤</strong>代價是 O(1)。這和動態陣列的道理一樣。`,"O(1) amortized per insert, with an occasional O(n) pause.":`每次插入均攤 O(1)，偶爾有一次 O(n) 的停頓。`,"Half full: comfortable.":`半滿：很寬鬆。`},t={"for each letter in word:":`對每個 word 中的字母:`,"if node has no child for it: add one":`如果 node 沒有對應它的孩子: 新增一個`,"node ← that child":`node ← 那個孩子`,"mark node as the end of a word":`把 node 標記為一個詞的結尾`,"if node has no child for it: return no":`如果 node 沒有對應它的孩子: 返回 否`,"return whether node is marked":`返回 node 是否被標記`,"One letter per node":`每個節點一個字母`,"A <strong>trie</strong> (say “try”) stores words by spelling them out down a tree, one letter per node. A word is a path from the root.":`<strong>字典樹</strong>（trie）把單詞沿著一棵樹逐個字母拼寫出來儲存，每個節點一個字母。一個單詞就是從根出發的一條路徑。`,"Here is CAT. The last letter is marked: that mark says “a word ends here”.":`這是 CAT。最後一個字母被標記了：這個標記的意思是「這裡有一個單詞結束」。`,"The way a dictionary’s page headers narrow down: C, then CA, then CAT.":`就像字典頁首一步步縮小範圍：C，然後 CA，然後 CAT。`,"Words stored":`已存單詞`,"Letters stored":`已存字母`,"of 3 written out":`/ 分開寫需 3 個`,"Shared beginnings":`共用的開頭`,"Add CAR. Walk down from the root: C is already there, and so is A. Only R is new.":`新增 CAR。從根往下走：C 已經在了，A 也在。只有 R 是新的。`,"Words that start the same way share their first nodes. The beginning is stored once, however many words use it.":`開頭相同的單詞共用最前面的節點。開頭只存一次，不管有多少個單詞用到它。`,"C: already here":`C：已經在了`,"A: already here":`A：已經在了`,"of 6 written out":`/ 分開寫需 6 個`,"A word inside a word":`單詞裡的單詞`,"Add DO and DOG. Nothing starts with D yet, so a new branch grows from the root.":`新增 DO 和 DOG。還沒有以 D 開頭的東西，所以從根長出一個新分支。`,"Both O and G are marked. DO ends at O even though the path carries on: the mark, not the end of the branch, is what makes it a word.":`O 和 G 都被標記了。DO 在 O 處結束，儘管路徑還在繼續：讓它成為單詞的是標記，而不是分支的盡頭。`,"of 11 written out":`/ 分開寫需 11 個`,"Look a word up":`查詢一個單詞`,"Is DOG in there? Follow D, O, G from the root. The path exists and ends on a marked node: yes.":`DOG 在裡面嗎？從根開始沿著 D、O、G 走。路徑存在，並且結束在一個被標記的節點上：在。`,"Three letters, three steps. It makes no difference whether the trie holds four words or four million.":`三個字母，三步。字典樹裡存了四個單詞還是四百萬個，都沒有區別。`,"O(length of the word). The number of words stored does not come into it.":`O(單詞的長度)。存了多少個單詞根本不影響。`,"G: a word ends here":`G：這裡有一個單詞結束`,"A path is not a word":`路徑不等於單詞`,"Is CA in there? C, then A: the path exists. But A is not marked, so no word ends there.":`CA 在裡面嗎？C，然後 A：路徑存在。但 A 沒有被標記，所以沒有單詞在那裡結束。`,"CA is not a word in this trie. It is a <strong>prefix</strong>: the start of words that are.":`CA 不是這棵字典樹裡的單詞。它是一個<strong>字首</strong>：一些單詞的開頭。`,"A: no word ends here":`A：沒有單詞在這裡結束`,"Everything that starts with…":`所有以……開頭的`,"And that is what a trie is best at. Walk to the end of a prefix, and every word that starts with it is in the subtree below: CAT and CAR.":`而這正是字典樹最擅長的。走到一個字首的末尾，所有以它開頭的單詞都在下面的子樹裡：CAT 和 CAR。`,"A hash table can tell you whether CAT is stored. It cannot tell you what begins with CA without checking every key.":`雜湊表能告訴你 CAT 有沒有存。但它不檢查每個鍵，就沒法告訴你有哪些以 CA 開頭。`,"Autocomplete, spell checkers, the routing tables that send packets across the internet.":`自動補全、拼寫檢查，還有把資料包送過網際網路的路由表。`,"starts with CA":`以 CA 開頭`,"The two words under C, A.":`C、A 下面的兩個單詞。`},n={"hash-tables":{"add up the codes of its letters":`把它各個字母的編碼加起來`,"return the sum mod the number of buckets":`返回 總和 mod 桶的數量`,"return bucket[hash(key)] = key":`返回 bucket[hash(key)] = key`,"Finding a key":`查詢一個鍵`,"Find without searching":`不用搜尋就能找到`,"An array finds things instantly, but only by index: “what is in cell 4?”. Real questions are about <em>names</em>: “is cat in here?”. Answering that from a list means checking it item by item.":`陣列能立刻找到東西，但只能按索引：「格子 4 裡是什麼？」。真正的問題是關於<em>名字</em>的：「cat 在這裡嗎？」。用列表回答這個問題，就得一項一項地檢查。`,"A <strong>hash table</strong> gets the speed of an index for any kind of key. It starts as a plain array of <strong>buckets</strong>.":`<strong>雜湊表</strong>讓任何型別的鍵都能擁有索引的速度。它一開始只是一個由<strong>桶</strong>組成的普通陣列。`,"Buckets looked in":`檢視的桶數`,"In a plain list":`在普通列表中`,"worst case":`最壞情況`,"Seven buckets, all empty.":`七個桶，全是空的。`,"Turn the key into a number":`把鍵變成數字`,Hash:`雜湊`,"The trick is a <strong>hash function</strong>: a fixed recipe that turns a key into a number. Here: add up the code numbers of the letters. For cat that is 99 + 97 + 116 = 312.":`訣竅是<strong>雜湊函式</strong>：一個把鍵變成數字的固定方法。這裡的方法是：把字母的編碼加起來。cat 是 99 + 97 + 116 = 312。`,"There is no bucket 312, so keep only the remainder after dividing by the number of buckets: 312 mod 7 = <strong>4</strong>.":`沒有 312 號桶，所以只保留除以桶數後的餘數：312 mod 7 = <strong>4</strong>。`,"The one rule":`唯一的規則`,"The same key must always give the same number. Nothing random, nothing that changes.":`同一個鍵必須總是得到同一個數字。不能有隨機的東西，也不能有會變的東西。`,"Store it there":`存到那裡`,"The hash says bucket 4, so cat goes in bucket 4. No other bucket was even looked at.":`雜湊說是 4 號桶，所以 cat 放進 4 號桶。其他桶連看都沒看。`,"More keys":`更多的鍵`,"Each key is hashed in the same way and goes straight to its own bucket: dog to 6, owl to 2.":`每個鍵都用同樣的方法雜湊，直接進入自己的桶：dog 進 6，owl 進 2。`,"The buckets fill in no particular order. A hash table does not keep its keys sorted, or in the order they arrived.":`桶不按任何特定順序填滿。雜湊表不會讓鍵保持有序，也不會保持它們到達的順序。`,"Look one up":`查詢一個`,"Is dog in the table? Hash it again. The recipe has not changed, so the answer is 6 again. Look in bucket 6: there it is.":`dog 在表裡嗎？再雜湊一次。方法沒變，所以答案還是 6。看看 6 號桶：就在那裡。`,"One bucket checked, however many keys are stored. That is the whole point.":`不管存了多少鍵，只檢查了一個桶。這正是關鍵所在。`,"O(1) on average, for storing and for finding. A list would be O(n).":`儲存和查詢平均都是 O(1)。列表則是 O(n)。`,"dog: found":`dog：找到了`,"A miss is just as quick":`找不到也一樣快`,"Is ant in the table? It hashes to 1, and bucket 1 is empty. If ant were stored, that is the only place it could be.":`ant 在表裡嗎？它雜湊到 1，而 1 號桶是空的。如果存了 ant，它只可能在那裡。`,"So it is not here. One look answered that too.":`所以它不在。看一次也回答了這個問題。`,"Two different keys can hash to the same bucket. What then is the next lesson.":`兩個不同的鍵可能雜湊到同一個桶。那時怎麼辦，是下一課的內容。`,"empty: not stored":`空：沒有存`},"collision-handling":{"put with chaining(key):":`鏈地址法 put(key):`,"add key to the list at bucket[hash(key)]":`把 key 加到 bucket[hash(key)] 處的連結串列裡`,"has with chaining(key):":`鏈地址法 has(key):`,"for each item in the list at bucket[hash(key)]:":`對每個 bucket[hash(key)] 處連結串列中的項:`,"if item = key: return yes":`如果 item = key: 返回 是`,"put with probing(key):":`線性探測 put(key):`,"while bucket[i] is taken:":`當 bucket[i] 已被佔用:`,"i ← the next bucket":`i ← 下一個桶`,"has with probing(key):":`線性探測 has(key):`,"if bucket[i] = key: return yes":`如果 bucket[i] = key: 返回 是`,"How full, how far":`有多滿，走多遠`,"Two keys, one bucket":`兩個鍵，一個桶`,"Store bee. Its letters add up to 300, and 300 mod 7 is 6. But dog is already in bucket 6.":`存入 bee。它的字母加起來是 300，300 mod 7 是 6。但 dog 已經在 6 號桶裡了。`,"This is a <strong>collision</strong>. It is not a bug in the hash function: there are far more possible keys than buckets, so some are bound to share.":`這就是<strong>衝突</strong>。這不是雜湊函式的 bug：可能的鍵遠比桶多，所以總有一些要共用。`,"in 7 buckets":`在 7 個桶中`,"Places looked at":`檢視的位置數`,"Bucket 6 is taken.":`6 號桶已被佔用。`,Chaining:`鏈地址法`,"Fix one":`解法一`,"One answer: let a bucket hold more than one key. Each bucket is the head of a small linked list, and a colliding key is simply added to it.":`一種解法：讓一個桶可以存多個鍵。每個桶都是一個小連結串列的頭，衝突的鍵直接加進去。`,"bee joins the chain at bucket 6, behind dog.":`bee 加入 6 號桶的鏈，排在 dog 後面。`,"Looking along a chain":`沿著鏈查詢`,"To find bee, hash it to bucket 6 as usual, then walk that bucket’s chain comparing keys: dog, no; bee, yes.":`要找 bee，照常把它雜湊到 6 號桶，然後沿著這個桶的鏈逐個比較鍵：dog，不是；bee，是。`,"Only the keys that collided are checked, never the whole table.":`只檢查發生衝突的鍵，從不檢查整張表。`,"O(1) to reach the bucket, plus the length of its chain. Short chains keep it fast.":`到達桶是 O(1)，再加上鍊的長度。鏈短就快。`,"bee: found":`bee：找到了`,"Open addressing":`開放定址`,"Fix two":`解法二`,"The other answer keeps one key per bucket, with no lists. Start again without bee, and store fox: it hashes to 4, where cat already is.":`另一種解法是每個桶只放一個鍵，不用連結串列。去掉 bee 重新開始，存入 fox：它雜湊到 4，而 cat 已經在那裡了。`,"With nowhere to chain, fox must find a different bucket.":`沒有鏈可掛，fox 必須找另一個桶。`,"Bucket 4 is taken.":`4 號桶已被佔用。`,"Probe for a free bucket":`探測空桶`,"The simplest rule is <strong>linear probing</strong>: try the next bucket along, and the next, until one is free. Bucket 5 is empty, so fox goes there.":`最簡單的規則是<strong>線性探測</strong>：試下一個桶，再下一個，直到找到空的。5 號桶是空的，所以 fox 放在那裡。`,"It is not where its hash said. That is fine, as long as lookups follow the same rule.":`它不在雜湊說的位置。這沒關係，只要查詢時遵循同樣的規則就行。`,"next free bucket":`下一個空桶`,"Find it the same way":`用同樣的方法查詢`,"Looking for fox: hash to 4, find cat, not it. Move along to 5: fox. An empty bucket would have meant “not stored”.":`查詢 fox：雜湊到 4，發現是 cat，不是它。往後移到 5：fox。如果遇到空桶，就意味著「沒有存」。`,"Either way, the fuller the table, the longer the chains or the probing. So tables watch how full they are, and move everything into a bigger array before it hurts.":`無論哪種方法，表越滿，鏈就越長，探測也越久。所以雜湊表會關注自己有多滿，在出問題之前把所有東西搬到一個更大的陣列裡。`,"Keep it under about two-thirds full. Past that, grow and re-hash every key.":`保持在大約三分之二滿以下。超過了就擴容，並重新雜湊每個鍵。`,"fox: found":`fox：找到了`,"Four of seven buckets used.":`七個桶用了四個。`},resizing:e,"sets-and-maps":{"seen ← an empty set":`seen ← 一個空集合`,"for each animal that goes by:":`對每個 經過的動物:`,"if seen has it: skip it":`如果 seen 裡有它: 跳過`,"else: add it to seen":`否則: 把它加進 seen`,"count ← an empty map":`count ← 一個空對映`,"if count has it: count[animal] ← count[animal] + 1":`如果 count 裡有它: count[animal] ← count[animal] + 1`,"else: count[animal] ← 1":`否則: count[animal] ← 1`,"A set":`集合`,"You rarely build a hash table yourself. You use the two things made from one. The first is a <strong>set</strong>: a collection of keys and nothing else.":`你很少需要自己實現雜湊表。你用的是用雜湊表做成的兩樣東西。第一樣是<strong>集合</strong>：只有鍵、別無他物的一組東西。`,"A set answers one question, fast: “is this in here?”. It has no order and no positions.":`集合能快速回答一個問題：「這個在裡面嗎？」。它沒有順序，也沒有位置。`,"This is a":`這是一個`,set:`集合`,"It holds":`它存著`,"Is it in?":`在裡面嗎？`,"Has a dog been seen? Hash the key, look in its bucket: yes.":`見過 dog 嗎？雜湊這個鍵，看它的桶：見過。`,"That is the lookup from the hash table lesson, and it is the whole of what a set is for.":`這就是雜湊表那一課裡的查詢，也是集合的全部用途。`,"O(1) on average, where searching a list is O(n).":`平均 O(1)，而在列表裡搜尋是 O(n)。`,"No duplicates":`沒有重複`,"Add cat again. It hashes to the bucket where cat already is, so there is nothing to do.":`再加一次 cat。它雜湊到 cat 已經在的那個桶，所以什麼都不用做。`,"A set holds each key once, however often it is added. Pour a list into a set and the repeats are gone.":`集合中每個鍵只存一次，不管加了多少次。把一個列表倒進集合，重複的就沒了。`,"already here":`已經在這裡`,"Still three keys.":`仍然是三個鍵。`,"A map":`對映`,"The second is a <strong>map</strong> (also called a dictionary): the same table, with a <strong>value</strong> kept beside each key.":`第二樣是<strong>對映</strong>（也叫字典）：同樣的表，只是每個鍵旁邊還存著一個<strong>值</strong>。`,"The key says which bucket. The value rides along with it. Here each animal carries how many times it has been seen.":`鍵決定放在哪個桶。值跟著它一起走。這裡每種動物都帶著它被見到的次數。`,map:`對映`,"Update a value":`更新一個值`,Map:`對映`,"Another dog goes by. Find dog by its key, read its value, write back one more.":`又一隻 dog 經過。按它的鍵找到 dog，讀出它的值，寫回多一的數。`,"Only the value changed. The key is still in the same bucket, because its hash has not changed.":`只有值變了。鍵還在同一個桶裡，因為它的雜湊沒有變。`,"Count anything":`什麼都能數`,"An ant, never seen before: it goes in with a count of 1. Those two cases, “seen it” and “new”, are the whole loop.":`一隻 ant，以前從沒見過：它以計數 1 加入。「見過」和「新的」這兩種情況，就是整個迴圈。`,"This is how words in a book are counted, how votes are tallied, how duplicates are found. One pass over the data, one quick step per item.":`數一本書裡的詞、統計選票、找出重複項，都是這樣做的。資料過一遍，每項一步快速操作。`,"Need “have I seen this?”: a set. Need “what goes with this?”: a map.":`需要「我見過這個嗎？」：用集合。需要「這個對應什麼？」：用對映。`},"bloom-filters":{"for each hash function h:":`對每個 雜湊函式 h:`,"if bits[h(key)] = 0: return no     // certain":`如果 bits[h(key)] = 0: 返回 否     // 確定`,"return maybe                           // probably":`返回 可能                           // 很可能`,"The filter":`過濾器`,"A set that forgets the keys":`一個會忘記鍵的集合`,"A hash set answers “is this in here?” exactly, but it has to store every key. A <strong>Bloom filter</strong> answers the same question in a sliver of the memory, by storing no keys at all: only a row of bits.":`雜湊集合能準確回答「這個在裡面嗎？」，但它得存下每個鍵。<strong>布隆過濾器</strong>只用一小部分記憶體就能回答同樣的問題，因為它根本不存鍵：只存一排位元。`,"The price is that it is sometimes wrong, in one direction only.":`代價是它有時會出錯，而且只會錯向一個方向。`,Added:`已新增`,"Asked about":`被詢問`,"Adding sets a few bits":`新增就是設定幾個位元`,"To add cat, run it through two different hash functions. They give 1 and 4. Set those two bits to 1.":`要新增 cat，就讓它透過兩個不同的雜湊函式。它們給出 1 和 4。把這兩個位元設為 1。`,"Nothing else about cat is kept.":`關於 cat 的其他資訊都不保留。`,"add cat":`新增 cat`,"Bits are shared":`位元是共用的`,"Add dog: its two hashes are 4 and 6. Bit 4 was already set by cat. That is fine: a bit only records that <em>something</em> set it.":`新增 dog：它的兩個雜湊值是 4 和 6。第 4 位元已經被 cat 設定過了。這沒關係：一個位元只記錄<em>有東西</em>設定過它。`,"add dog":`新增 dog`,"A zero means no":`0 表示不在`,"Is bee in the set? Its hashes are 3 and 6. Bit 3 is 0. If bee had ever been added, that bit would be 1.":`bee 在集合裡嗎？它的雜湊值是 3 和 6。第 3 位元是 0。如果 bee 曾經被新增過，這個位元就會是 1。`,"So bee is <strong>definitely not</strong> there. A Bloom filter never says no by mistake.":`所以 bee <strong>肯定不</strong>在裡面。布隆過濾器從不會錯誤地說「不在」。`,"0: never added":`0：從未新增`,"All ones means maybe":`全是 1 表示可能`,"Is owl in the set? Its hashes are 1 and 6. Both bits are 1, so the filter says yes. But owl was never added: cat set bit 1 and dog set bit 6.":`owl 在集合裡嗎？它的雜湊值是 1 和 6。兩個位元都是 1，所以過濾器說在。但 owl 從沒被新增過：第 1 位元是 cat 設定的，第 6 位元是 dog 設定的。`,"This is a <strong>false positive</strong>. A yes only ever means “maybe”.":`這就是<strong>假陽性</strong>。「在」永遠只意味著「可能在」。`,"both set: maybe":`都已設定：可能`,maybe:`可能`,"Wrong this time.":`這次錯了。`,"A cheap first check":`便宜的初步檢查`,"That one-sided error is very useful. Put the filter in front of something slow, such as a disk or a network call. A “no” skips the slow step entirely; a “maybe” goes on to the real check.":`這種單向的錯誤非常有用。把過濾器放在慢的東西前面，比如磁碟或網路呼叫。「不在」就完全跳過慢的步驟；「可能」才繼續做真正的檢查。`,"More bits and more hash functions make false positives rarer. Keys cannot be removed, since a bit may belong to several.":`位元越多、雜湊函式越多，假陽性就越少。鍵不能刪除，因為一個位元可能屬於好幾個鍵。`,"Databases checking whether a file could hold a key; browsers checking a URL against a list of unsafe sites.":`資料庫檢查一個檔案是否可能包含某個鍵；瀏覽器把網址和不安全網站列表比對。`,"Three bits stand for two keys of any size.":`三個位元代表了兩個任意大小的鍵。`},"binary-trees":{"left       // another node, or nothing":`left       // 另一個節點，或者空`,"right      // another node, or nothing":`right      // 另一個節點，或者空`,"root       // the one node with no parent":`root       // 唯一沒有父節點的節點`,"This tree":`這棵樹`,"One node, two children":`一個節點，兩個孩子`,"A linked-list node points at one other node. Give a node <strong>two</strong> pointers, <em>left</em> and <em>right</em>, and the list becomes a tree.":`連結串列的節點指向另一個節點。給節點<strong>兩個</strong>指標，<em>left</em> 和 <em>right</em>，連結串列就變成了樹。`,"A is the <strong>root</strong>: the one node nothing points at. B and C are its <strong>children</strong>, and A is their <strong>parent</strong>.":`A 是<strong>根</strong>：唯一沒有東西指向的節點。B 和 C 是它的<strong>孩子</strong>，A 是它們的<strong>父節點</strong>。`,"A family tree drawn with the oldest ancestor at the top.":`一張家譜，最老的祖先畫在最上面。`,"the root":`根`,Leaves:`葉子`,"no children":`沒有孩子`,"longest way down":`最長的向下路徑`,"It keeps branching":`它不斷分叉`,"Each child can have two children of its own, and so on down.":`每個孩子還可以有自己的兩個孩子，一直往下。`,"A node with no children is a <strong>leaf</strong>. D, E, F and G are the leaves here: every way down from the root ends at one.":`沒有孩子的節點叫<strong>葉子</strong>。這裡 D、E、F 和 G 是葉子：從根往下的每條路都終止於一片葉子。`,"Depth and height":`深度與高度`,Measure:`測量`,"A node’s <strong>depth</strong> is how many branches lie between it and the root. The root is at depth 0, its children at depth 1.":`節點的<strong>深度</strong>是它和根之間有多少條樹枝。根的深度是 0，它的孩子的深度是 1。`,"The tree’s <strong>height</strong> is the depth of its deepest leaf: here, 2. Most of what a tree costs to use depends on its height.":`樹的<strong>高度</strong>是它最深的葉子的深度：這裡是 2。使用一棵樹的大部分代價都取決於它的高度。`,"Trees inside trees":`樹中有樹`,"Look only at B and everything below it. That is a tree too, with B as its root: a <strong>subtree</strong>.":`只看 B 和它下面的一切。那也是一棵樹，以 B 為根：一棵<strong>子樹</strong>。`,"Every node is the root of its own subtree. This is why so much tree code is recursive: do the job for a node, then for its left subtree, then its right.":`每個節點都是它自己那棵子樹的根。這就是為什麼那麼多處理樹的程式碼都是遞迴的：為一個節點做事，然後為它的左子樹做，再為它的右子樹做。`,"a subtree":`一棵子樹`,"Counting only the subtree under B.":`只計算 B 下面的子樹。`,"How much fits":`能裝多少`,Growth:`增長`,"Every level can hold twice as many nodes as the one above: 1, 2, 4, 8. One more level roughly doubles the whole tree.":`每一層能裝的節點數是上一層的兩倍：1、2、4、8。多一層，整棵樹大約翻一倍。`,"So a full tree of height 3 holds 15 nodes, and one of height 20 holds over two million. A lot of data is only a few steps from the root.":`所以高度為 3 的滿樹能裝 15 個節點，高度為 20 的能裝兩百多萬個。大量資料離根只有幾步之遙。`,"n nodes can fit in a height of about log₂ n. That is where tree speed comes from.":`n 個節點可以裝進大約 log₂ n 的高度。樹的速度就來自這裡。`,"Not always tidy":`不總是整齊的`,"Nothing says a binary tree must be full. “Binary” only promises <em>at most</em> two children.":`沒有規定二元樹必須是滿的。「二元」只保證<em>最多</em>兩個孩子。`,"This one has five nodes and is as tall as the fifteen-node tree was. Taken to the extreme, with one child everywhere, a tree is just a linked list.":`這棵樹有五個節點，卻和那棵十五個節點的樹一樣高。走到極端，每處都只有一個孩子，樹就只是一個連結串列。`,"Same height, a third of the nodes.":`同樣的高度，三分之一的節點。`},"tree-traversals":{"if node is nothing: return":`如果 node 為空: 返回`,"visit node             // here: pre-order":`訪問 node             // 在這裡：前序`,"visit node             // here: in-order":`訪問 node             // 在這裡：中序`,"visit node             // here: post-order":`訪問 node             // 在這裡：後序`,"put root in a queue":`把 root 放進一個佇列`,"take a node from the front, visit it":`從隊首取出一個節點，訪問它`,"put its children at the back":`把它的孩子放到隊尾`,"Orders of visiting":`訪問順序`,"Visit every node":`訪問每個節點`,"A list has one obvious order to read it in. A tree does not: at every node there are two ways to go.":`列表只有一種顯而易見的讀法。樹沒有：在每個節點上都有兩條路可走。`,"A <strong>traversal</strong> is a rule for visiting every node exactly once. There are four standard ones, and they differ only in <em>when</em> each node gets its turn.":`<strong>遍歷</strong>是讓每個節點恰好被訪問一次的規則。標準的有四種，它們唯一的區別是每個節點<em>什麼時候</em>輪到。`,"Pre-order":`前序`,"In-order":`中序`,"Post-order":`後序`,"Level-order":`層序`,"Seven nodes, many possible orders.":`七個節點，可能的順序有很多。`,"Depth first":`深度優先`,"Walk the tree depth first: down the left as far as possible, back up, then down the right.":`深度優先地走這棵樹：沿左邊儘量往下走，退回來，再往右邊下去。`,"<strong>Pre-order</strong> counts a node the moment the walk first reaches it, before either subtree. Parents always come before their children.":`<strong>前序</strong>在第一次走到一個節點時就計數它，早於它的兩棵子樹。父節點總是排在孩子前面。`,"Good for":`適用於`,"Copying a tree, or writing it out: you meet each parent before you need to attach its children.":`複製一棵樹，或者把它寫出來：在需要掛上孩子之前，你已經先遇到了它們的父節點。`,"The walk is exactly the same. Watch the cursor: it takes the same path round the tree.":`走法完全一樣。看著遊標：它繞著樹走的是同一條路。`,"<strong>In-order</strong> counts a node on the way back up from its left subtree, before going down the right: left, node, right.":`<strong>中序</strong>在從左子樹返回的路上計數一個節點，然後才往右下去：左、節點、右。`,"A binary search tree: in-order visits its values from smallest to largest.":`二元搜尋樹：中序遍歷會從小到大訪問它的值。`,"Same walk a third time. <strong>Post-order</strong> counts a node only when the walk is leaving it for good, after both subtrees are done.":`第三次走同樣的路。<strong>後序</strong>只在徹底離開一個節點時才計數它，也就是兩棵子樹都處理完之後。`,"Children always come before their parent, and the root comes last.":`孩子總是排在父節點前面，根排在最後。`,"Deleting a tree, or adding up sizes: a node is handled once everything under it is finished.":`刪除一棵樹，或者累加大小：一個節點要等它下面的一切都處理完才處理。`,"Breadth first":`廣度優先`,"The fourth order does not follow the branches at all. It reads the tree like a page: top level first, each level left to right.":`第四種順序完全不沿著樹枝走。它像讀一頁書那樣讀樹：先讀最上層，每層從左到右。`,"It needs a <strong>queue</strong> to remember whose children are next, where the depth-first walks use the call stack.":`它需要一個<strong>佇列</strong>來記住接下來輪到誰的孩子，而深度優先的走法用的是呼叫堆疊。`,"Finding the nearest thing to the root: it reaches closer nodes before farther ones.":`找離根最近的東西：它會先到達較近的節點，再到達較遠的。`},"lowest-common-ancestor":{"if node is nothing, or is p, or is q:":`如果 node 為空，或者是 p，或者是 q:`,"if both found something:":`如果 兩邊都找到了東西:`,"return node            // p and q are on different sides":`返回 node            // p 和 q 在不同的兩邊`,"return whichever one did":`返回 找到東西的那一邊`,"Where two paths join":`兩條路在哪裡匯合`,"In a family tree, who is the closest ancestor two people share? In a folder tree, what is the smallest folder that contains two files?":`在家譜裡，兩個人共有的最近的祖先是誰？在資料夾樹裡，同時包含兩個檔案的最小資料夾是哪個？`,"Both are the same question: the <strong>lowest common ancestor</strong> of two nodes.":`兩個都是同一個問題：兩個節點的<strong>最近公共祖先</strong>。`,"The two nodes":`這兩個節點`,"Lowest common ancestor":`最近公共祖先`,Ancestors:`祖先`,"A node’s ancestors are everything on the way from it up to the root. For D that is B, then A.":`一個節點的祖先，是從它往上到根的路上的一切。D 的祖先是 B，然後是 A。`,"Every node counts as an ancestor of itself.":`每個節點都算是它自己的祖先。`,"D’s ancestors: D, B, A.":`D 的祖先：D、B、A。`,"The first one they share":`它們共有的第一個`,"Take D and G. D’s ancestors are D, B, A. G’s are G, C, A. Going up from each, the first node on both lists is A.":`取 D 和 G。D 的祖先是 D、B、A。G 的是 G、C、A。從各自往上走，第一個同時出現在兩個列表裡的節點是 A。`,"D is in A’s left subtree and G in its right. That is the test: the lowest common ancestor is where the two nodes fall on <em>different sides</em>.":`D 在 A 的左子樹裡，G 在右子樹裡。這就是判斷方法：最近公共祖先就是兩個節點落在<em>不同兩邊</em>的地方。`,"they split here":`它們在這裡分開`,"D and G":`D 和 G`,"Lower down":`再往下`,"Now D and E. Both are under B, one on each side of it. So B is their lowest common ancestor. A is also a common ancestor, but it is not the lowest.":`現在是 D 和 E。兩個都在 B 下面，一邊一個。所以 B 是它們的最近公共祖先。A 也是公共祖先，但不是最近的。`,"D and E":`D 和 E`,"One above the other":`一個在另一個上面`,"Edge case":`邊界情況`,"What about B and E? E is underneath B, so B is an ancestor of both, itself included. The answer is B.":`B 和 E 呢？E 在 B 下面，所以 B 是兩者的祖先，包括它自己。答案是 B。`,"The search stops as soon as it reaches either node: whatever is below it cannot change the answer.":`搜尋一到達其中任何一個節點就停止：它下面的東西都不會改變答案。`,"its own ancestor":`是它自己的祖先`,"B and E":`B 和 E`,"One walk of the tree":`走一遍樹`,"A single depth-first walk answers it: each node reports upward whether one of the two was found beneath it, and the first node to hear from both sides is the answer.":`一次深度優先遍歷就能回答：每個節點向上報告它下面是否找到了兩者之一，第一個從兩邊都收到訊息的節點就是答案。`,"In a binary search tree it is easier still: walk down from the root until the two values fall on opposite sides.":`在二元搜尋樹裡就更簡單了：從根往下走，直到兩個值落在相反的兩邊。`,"O(n) in any tree, O(height) in a search tree.":`任何樹都是 O(n)，搜尋樹是 O(高度)。`},"binary-search-trees":{"if node is nothing: return not found":`如果 node 為空: 返回 未找到`,"if x = node.value: return node":`如果 x = node.value: 返回 node`,"if x < node.value: return search(node.left, x)":`如果 x < node.value: 返回 search(node.left, x)`,"return search(node.right, x)":`返回 search(node.right, x)`,"if node is nothing: return a new node holding x":`如果 node 為空: 返回 一個存放 x 的新節點`,"if x < node.value: node.left ← insert(node.left, x)":`如果 x < node.value: node.left ← insert(node.left, x)`,"else: node.right ← insert(node.right, x)":`否則: node.right ← insert(node.right, x)`,"Smaller left, bigger right":`左邊小，右邊大`,"A <strong>binary search tree</strong> is a binary tree with one rule. At every node, everything in its left subtree is smaller and everything in its right subtree is bigger.":`<strong>二元搜尋樹</strong>是帶有一條規則的二元樹。在每個節點上，左子樹裡的一切都更小，右子樹裡的一切都更大。`,"Check it: left of 50 are 20, 30, 40. Right of it are 60, 70, 80. The same holds at 30 and at 70.":`檢查一下：50 的左邊是 20、30、40。右邊是 60、70、80。在 30 和 70 上也是如此。`,"The rule covers whole subtrees, not just the two children.":`這條規則管的是整棵子樹，而不只是兩個孩子。`,"Nodes in the tree":`樹中的節點`,"Nodes looked at":`檢視的節點`,"To find 60, start at the root and compare. 60 is bigger than 50, so it can only be on the right: the entire left half is ruled out at once.":`要找 60，就從根開始比較。60 比 50 大，所以它只可能在右邊：整個左半邊一下子就被排除了。`,"60 is smaller than 70, so go left. There it is. Three nodes looked at, out of seven.":`60 比 70 小，所以往左走。就在那裡。七個節點只看了三個。`,"One comparison per level: O(height). In a well-shaped tree that is O(log n).":`每層比較一次：O(高度)。在形狀好的樹裡，那就是 O(log n)。`,"60 > 50: go right":`60 > 50：往右`,"60 < 70: go left":`60 < 70：往左`,"found 60":`找到 60`,"It is binary search, with the halving built into the shape.":`這就是二分搜尋，只是對半分已經內建在形狀裡了。`,"A miss":`找不到`,"Look for 45. Left at 50, right at 30, right at 40, and there is no node there.":`找 45。在 50 往左，在 30 往右，在 40 往右，那裡沒有節點。`,"That empty place is the only one 45 could have been in, so it is not in the tree. No need to look anywhere else.":`那個空位是 45 唯一可能在的地方，所以它不在樹裡。不用再去別處找了。`,"45 < 50: go left":`45 < 50：往左`,"45 > 30: go right":`45 > 30：往右`,"45 > 40: go right":`45 > 40：往右`,"nothing here":`這裡什麼都沒有`,"Inserting is searching, then filling the gap. The search for 45 ended at an empty place below 40: that is exactly where 45 belongs.":`插入就是先搜尋，再填空。搜尋 45 停在了 40 下面的一個空位：45 正應該放在那裡。`,"A new node always goes in as a leaf. Nothing else has to move.":`新節點總是作為葉子放進去。其他什麼都不用動。`,"In order means sorted":`中序就是有序`,Property:`性質`,"Walk the tree in-order: left subtree, node, right subtree. Because smaller is always left, the values come out from smallest to largest.":`中序遍歷這棵樹：左子樹、節點、右子樹。因為小的總在左邊，值就會從小到大地出來。`,"So a binary search tree is a sorted collection that is also quick to search and to add to.":`所以二元搜尋樹是一個有序的集合，同時搜尋和新增都很快。`,"It depends on the shape":`這取決於形狀`,"Now build a tree by inserting 10, 20, 30, 40 in that order. Each is bigger than everything before it, so each goes to the right of the last.":`現在按 10、20、30、40 的順序插入來建一棵樹。每個都比之前的所有值大，所以每個都放在上一個的右邊。`,"It obeys the rule, and it is useless: a linked list with extra pointers. Searching it is O(n).":`它遵守規則，但毫無用處：一個多帶了指標的連結串列。在它裡面搜尋是 O(n)。`,"Keeping a tree short however the values arrive is what balanced trees are for.":`不管值以什麼順序到來，都讓樹保持矮，這正是平衡樹的用途。`,"Finding 40 looks at every node.":`找 40 要看每一個節點。`},"bst-deletion":{"if it has no children:":`如果 它沒有孩子:`,"unhook it":`把它解開`,"else if it has one child:":`否則，如果它有一個孩子:`,"put that child in its place":`讓那個孩子頂替它的位置`,"next ← the smallest node in its right subtree":`next ← 它右子樹中最小的節點`,"copy next's value into the node":`把 next 的值複製到這個節點裡`,"delete next              // which has at most one child":`刪除 next              // 它最多隻有一個孩子`,"Removing a node":`刪除一個節點`,"Three cases":`三種情況`,"Taking a value out of a binary search tree is harder than putting one in, because the hole has to be filled without breaking the order.":`從二元搜尋樹裡取出一個值，比放進一個值更難，因為必須在不破壞順序的情況下填上空位。`,"What to do depends on how many children the node has: none, one or two.":`怎麼做取決於這個節點有幾個孩子：零個、一個還是兩個。`,"This case":`這種情況`,"No children":`沒有孩子`,"Case one":`情況一`,"20 is a leaf. Nothing hangs below it, so nothing can be disturbed: unhook it from its parent and it is gone.":`20 是葉子。它下面什麼都沒掛，所以什麼都不會受影響：把它從父節點上解開，它就沒了。`,"20 unhooked":`20 已解開`,"One child":`一個孩子`,"Case two":`情況二`,"60 has a single child, 65. Everything under 60 already belongs on that side of 70, so the child can simply move up into its place.":`60 只有一個孩子，65。60 下面的一切本來就屬於 70 的這一邊，所以這個孩子可以直接上移到它的位置。`,"takes 60’s place":`頂替 60 的位置`,"one child":`一個孩子`,"Two children: find a stand-in":`兩個孩子：找一個替身`,"Case three":`情況三`,"Now delete 50, the root. It has two subtrees and only one place for them to hang.":`現在刪除根 50。它有兩棵子樹，卻只有一個地方能掛。`,"So the node is kept and its <em>value</em> replaced, with the next value up in order: go right once, then left as far as possible. That is 65. It is bigger than everything on the left and smaller than everything else on the right.":`所以保留這個節點，替換它的<em>值</em>，換成按順序緊接著的下一個值：往右走一步，再儘量往左走。那是 65。它比左邊的一切都大，又比右邊其餘的一切都小。`,"right once":`往右一步`,"then left to the end":`再一直往左`,"two children":`兩個孩子`,"65 takes the root’s place. The stand-in was itself easy to remove: being the leftmost of its subtree, it had no left child, so it was one of the first two cases.":`65 頂替了根的位置。替身本身很容易刪除：作為它所在子樹最左邊的節點，它沒有左孩子，所以屬於前兩種情況之一。`,"Still in order":`仍然有序`,"Walk what is left in order: 30, 40, 65, 70, 80. Still sorted, so it is still a search tree.":`按中序走一遍剩下的：30、40、65、70、80。仍然有序，所以它仍然是搜尋樹。`,"Each case walked at most one path down the tree.":`每種情況最多沿樹往下走一條路徑。`,"O(height), like search and insert.":`O(高度)，和搜尋、插入一樣。`,"Three removed, order intact.":`刪除了三個，順序完好。`},"balanced-trees":{"insert x as in any search tree":`像在任何搜尋樹中一樣插入 x`,"on the way back up, at each node:":`在返回的路上，在每個節點:`,"if one side is two taller than the other:":`如果 一邊比另一邊高出兩層:`,"rotate the node towards the short side":`把節點往矮的一邊旋轉`,"node.right ← child.left      // the middle subtree changes sides":`node.right ← child.left      // 中間的子樹換到另一邊`,"return child                 // it takes the node's place":`返回 child                 // 它頂替這個節點的位置`,"How tall":`有多高`,"A lopsided tree":`一棵歪斜的樹`,"Insert 10, 20, 30 into a search tree and it comes out as a chain. It is as tall as it could possibly be.":`把 10、20、30 插入一棵搜尋樹，它就成了一條鏈。它已經高到不能再高了。`,"Everything a search tree does costs its height, so this is the shape to avoid. A <strong>balanced</strong> tree fixes its own shape as it grows.":`搜尋樹做的每件事都取決於它的高度，所以這正是要避免的形狀。<strong>平衡</strong>樹會在長大的過程中自己調整形狀。`,"right side is 2 taller":`右邊高出 2 層`,"Shortest possible":`最矮可能的高度`,"A rotation":`旋轉`,Repair:`修復`,"The fix is a <strong>rotation</strong>. 20 moves up to become the root, and 10 comes down to be its left child.":`修復方法是<strong>旋轉</strong>。20 上移成為根，10 下來成為它的左孩子。`,"The order is untouched: 10 is still left of 20, and 30 is still right of it. It is the same search tree, one level shorter.":`順序沒有被破壞：10 仍在 20 的左邊，30 仍在它的右邊。它還是同一棵搜尋樹，只是矮了一層。`,"A rotation rewrites a few pointers. It is O(1), whatever the size of the tree.":`一次旋轉只改寫幾個指標。它是 O(1)，不管樹有多大。`,"Insert, then check":`插入，然後檢查`,"Carry on: insert 40, then 50. Each goes in at the bottom right, as usual.":`繼續：插入 40，然後 50。每個都照常放到右下方。`,"After 50, look at 30. Its right side is two levels tall and its left side is empty: out of balance.":`插入 50 之後，看看 30。它的右邊有兩層高，左邊是空的：失去平衡了。`,"Repair where it broke":`在出問題的地方修復`,"Rotate at 30, the lowest node that is out of balance. 40 moves up into its place, with 30 and 50 either side.":`在 30 處旋轉，它是最低的失衡節點。40 上移到它的位置，30 和 50 分在兩邊。`,"Only that corner of the tree changed. Everything above it is as it was.":`只有樹的那個角落變了。它上面的一切都和原來一樣。`,"A subtree changes sides":`一棵子樹換邊`,"Insert 60, and now the root itself is lopsided: one level on its left, three on its right. Rotate at 20.":`插入 60，現在根本身歪了：左邊一層，右邊三層。在 20 處旋轉。`,"40 becomes the root. It already had a left child, 30, and that place is now needed for 20. So 30 moves across to hang under 20, which is where a value between 20 and 40 belongs.":`40 成為根。它原本就有一個左孩子 30，而那個位置現在需要留給 20。所以 30 挪過去掛在 20 下面，那正是介於 20 和 40 之間的值該在的地方。`,"Short, whatever arrives":`不管來什麼，都保持矮`,"Six values went in already sorted, the worst case for a plain search tree, and the result is as short as a tree of six can be.":`六個值按已排好的順序放進來，這對普通搜尋樹來說是最壞的情況，而結果卻是六個節點的樹所能達到的最矮形狀。`,"With the repair built into insert and delete, the height stays near log₂ n. A million values: about 20 levels.":`把修復內建到插入和刪除中，高度就保持在 log₂ n 附近。一百萬個值：大約 20 層。`,"AVL trees and red-black trees work this way. They are behind most sorted maps and sets.":`AVL 樹和紅黑樹就是這樣工作的。大多數有序對映和有序集合背後都是它們。`,"Unrepaired, this would be a chain of height 5.":`如果不修復，這會是一條高度為 5 的鏈。`},tries:t,"segment-trees":{"if range is one cell: node ← that value":`如果 range 只有一個格子: node ← 那個值`,"else: node ← build(left half) + build(right half)":`否則: node ← build(左半) + build(右半)`,"if the node's range is inside range: return node":`如果 節點的範圍在 range 之內: 返回 node`,"if it is outside: return 0":`如果 它在範圍之外: 返回 0`,"return query(left child) + query(right child)":`返回 query(左孩子) + query(右孩子)`,"change that leaf":`修改那片葉子`,"recompute every node on the way up to the root":`重新計算往上到根的路上的每個節點`,"Range sums that keep changing":`不斷變化的區間和`,"Prefix sums answer “what do cells i to j add up to?” instantly. But change one value and every total after it is wrong: an update costs O(n).":`字首和能立刻回答「格子 i 到 j 加起來是多少？」。但改一個值，它後面的每個累計和就都錯了：一次更新要 O(n)。`,"When the data keeps changing, something else is needed. Start with the array itself: 2, 5, 1, 4.":`資料一直在變的時候，就需要別的東西。先從陣列本身開始：2、5、1、4。`,"Nodes touched":`觸及的節點`,"Sums of pairs, then pairs of pairs":`兩兩相加，再兩兩相加`,"Above each pair of cells put their sum: 7 and 5. Above those, their sum: 12.":`在每對格子上方放上它們的和：7 和 5。再在它們上方放上它們的和：12。`,"Every node holds the total of the stretch of the array beneath it. This is a <strong>segment tree</strong>.":`每個節點都存著它下方那一段陣列的總和。這就是<strong>線段樹</strong>。`,"Built once, in O(n).":`構建一次，O(n)。`,"A query takes whole nodes":`查詢使用整個節點`,"What do cells 0 to 2 add up to? Cells 0 and 1 are covered exactly by the node 7, so take it whole. Cell 2 is the leaf 1.":`格子 0 到 2 加起來是多少？格子 0 和 1 正好被節點 7 覆蓋，所以整個拿來。格子 2 是葉子 1。`,"7 + 1 = 8, from two nodes instead of three cells. On a big array a query never needs more than about two nodes per level.":`7 + 1 = 8，用了兩個節點而不是三個格子。在大陣列上，一次查詢每層最多只需要兩個左右的節點。`,"An update starts at a leaf":`更新從一片葉子開始`,Update:`更新`,"Change cell 1 from 5 to 6. Only one leaf holds that value.":`把格子 1 從 5 改成 6。只有一片葉子存著這個值。`,"was 5":`原來是 5`,"Then fixes the path above it":`然後修正它上方的路徑`,"The nodes that include cell 1 are the ones on the way up to the root: 7 becomes 8, and 12 becomes 13.":`包含格子 1 的節點，就是往上到根的路上的那些：7 變成 8，12 變成 13。`,"Nothing else in the tree covers that cell, so nothing else changes.":`樹裡沒有別的節點覆蓋這個格子，所以別的都不變。`,"Quick both ways":`兩種操作都快`,"A query and an update each touch a handful of nodes per level, and there are about log n levels.":`查詢和更新每層都只觸及幾個節點，而一共大約有 log n 層。`,"Swap the + for “smaller of” or “bigger of” and the same tree answers range minimum or range maximum.":`把 + 換成「較小的」或「較大的」，同一棵樹就能回答區間最小值或區間最大值。`,"O(log n) to query and to update. Prefix sums are O(1) and O(n).":`查詢和更新都是 O(log n)。字首和是 O(1) 和 O(n)。`},"binary-heaps":{"put x in the next free place":`把 x 放到下一個空位`,"while x is smaller than its parent:":`當 x 比它的父節點小:`,"swap them                // sift up":`交換它們                // 上浮`,"keep the root to hand back":`留住根，準備交回去`,"move the last item to the root":`把最後一項移到根`,"while it is bigger than a child:":`當 它比某個孩子大:`,"swap it with its smaller child   // sift down":`把它和較小的孩子交換   // 下沉`,"return what was kept":`返回 留住的那個`,"The heap":`堆積`,"Smallest on top":`最小的在頂上`,"A <strong>heap</strong> is a binary tree with one rule: every node is smaller than its children. So the smallest value of all is always at the root.":`<strong>堆積</strong>是帶有一條規則的二元樹：每個節點都比它的孩子小。所以所有值中最小的，總在根上。`,"That is the only promise. 9 is on the left and 8 on the right; a heap is not sorted, and it is not a search tree. It is just enough order to find the minimum instantly.":`這是它唯一的承諾。9 在左邊，8 在右邊；堆積不是有序的，也不是搜尋樹。它的順序剛好夠立刻找到最小值。`,"Two kinds":`兩種`,"This is a min-heap. Turn the rule round, parents bigger than children, and it is a max-heap.":`這是最小堆積。把規則反過來，父節點比孩子大，就是最大堆積。`,"the smallest":`最小的`,"As an array":`作為陣列`,Smallest:`最小`,Items:`項`,"Really an array":`其實是陣列`,"A heap is always filled level by level, left to right, with no gaps. Number the nodes in that order and the tree fits in a plain array: no pointers at all.":`堆積總是一層一層、從左到右地填滿，不留空隙。按這個順序給節點編號，樹就能放進一個普通陣列：完全不需要指標。`,"The node at index i has its children at 2i + 1 and 2i + 2, and its parent at (i − 1) ÷ 2, rounded down. Index 1 holds 5; its children are at 3 and 4: 9 and 7.":`索引 i 處節點的孩子在 2i + 1 和 2i + 2，父節點在 (i − 1) ÷ 2，向下取整。索引 1 存著 5；它的孩子在 3 和 4：9 和 7。`,"Read the tree level by level.":`一層一層地讀這棵樹。`,"Insert at the end":`插在末尾`,"To add 4, put it in the next free place: the end of the array, the next gap in the bottom row.":`要新增 4，就把它放到下一個空位：陣列的末尾，也就是最底一行的下一個空隙。`,"The shape is right, but the rule is broken. 4 is smaller than its parent, 8.":`形狀是對的，但規則被破壞了。4 比它的父節點 8 小。`,"4 < 8: out of order":`4 < 8：順序不對`,"Sift up":`上浮`,"Swap 4 with its parent. Now compare again, one level up: 4 is bigger than 3, so it stops there.":`把 4 和它的父節點交換。然後在上一層再比較一次：4 比 3 大，所以停在那裡。`,"A new item only ever climbs its own path towards the root. The rest of the heap is never touched.":`新項只會沿著它自己通往根的路徑往上爬。堆積的其餘部分從不被碰到。`,"At most one swap per level: O(log n).":`每層最多交換一次：O(log n)。`,"4 > 3: stop":`4 > 3：停止`,"Take the smallest":`取出最小的`,"The smallest is the root, so taking it is easy. But that leaves a hole at the top.":`最小的就是根，所以取它很容易。但這會在頂上留下一個洞。`,"Fill it with the last item, 8. That keeps the shape complete, and breaks the rule again: 8 is bigger than both its children.":`用最後一項 8 填上它。這樣形狀保持完整，但規則又被破壞了：8 比它的兩個孩子都大。`,"too big for the top":`放在頂上太大了`,"Handed back: 3.":`交回：3。`,"Sift down":`下沉`,"Swap 8 with its <em>smaller</em> child, 4, so that the new parent is smaller than both. Then look again: 8 is smaller than 12, so it stops.":`把 8 和它<em>較小</em>的孩子 4 交換，這樣新的父節點比兩個孩子都小。然後再看：8 比 12 小，所以停止。`,"The next smallest value is now on top, ready to be taken.":`下一個最小的值現在在頂上，隨時可以取走。`,"O(log n) to insert or remove, O(1) to look at the smallest.":`插入或刪除 O(log n)，檢視最小值 O(1)。`,"8 < 12: stop":`8 < 12：停止`},"building-a-heap":{"for i from the last parent back to the root:":`對於 i 從最後一個父節點倒著到根:`,"sift a[i] down":`讓 a[i] 下沉`,"while a[i] is bigger than a child:":`當 a[i] 比某個孩子大:`,"swap it with its smaller child":`把它和較小的孩子交換`,"Any array is a tree":`任何陣列都是一棵樹`,"Read level by level, any array is a complete binary tree. This one, 9 7 8 3 5 4, is just not a heap yet: parents are bigger than their children all over the place.":`一層一層地讀，任何陣列都是一棵完全二元樹。這個陣列 9 7 8 3 5 4 只是還不是堆積：到處都是父節點比孩子大。`,"It could be fixed by inserting the items one at a time, at O(n log n). There is a faster way.":`可以一次插入一項來修好它，代價是 O(n log n)。還有更快的方法。`,"Swaps so far":`已交換次數`,"Start at the last parent":`從最後一個父節點開始`,"The leaves need no work: a node with no children cannot break the rule. So begin with the last node that <em>has</em> a child, 8, and sift it down.":`葉子不需要處理：沒有孩子的節點不可能破壞規則。所以從最後一個<em>有</em>孩子的節點 8 開始，讓它下沉。`,"8 is bigger than its child 4. Swap them.":`8 比它的孩子 4 大。交換它們。`,"8 > 4: swapped":`8 > 4：已交換`,"Work backwards":`倒著往前做`,"The parent before that is 7. Its children are 3 and 5; swap with the smaller, 3.":`再往前的父節點是 7。它的孩子是 3 和 5；和較小的 3 交換。`,"Each small subtree is made into a heap before the node above it is looked at.":`每棵小子樹都先變成堆積，然後才去看它上面的節點。`,"7 > 3: swapped":`7 > 3：已交換`,"The root sinks":`根往下沉`,"Last, the root. 9 is bigger than both children, 3 and 4. It swaps with the smaller, 3.":`最後是根。9 比它的兩個孩子 3 和 4 都大。它和較小的 3 交換。`,"Both subtrees were already heaps, so this is an ordinary sift-down.":`兩棵子樹都已經是堆積了，所以這只是普通的下沉。`,"still too big":`還是太大`,"As far as it needs to":`需要多遠就走多遠`,"9 is still bigger than its new children, 7 and 5. Swap with 5, and it reaches the bottom.":`9 還是比它的新孩子 7 和 5 大。和 5 交換，它就到了底部。`,"Every parent is now smaller than its children. It is a heap.":`現在每個父節點都比它的孩子小。這是一個堆積了。`,"Cheaper than it looks":`比看起來便宜`,"Four swaps for six items. The reason it is fast: half the nodes are leaves and do nothing, a quarter can sink at most one level, an eighth at most two.":`六個項交換了四次。它快的原因是：一半的節點是葉子，什麼都不用做；四分之一最多下沉一層，八分之一最多兩層。`,"Only the root can travel the whole height. Added up, the work is proportional to n, not n log n.":`只有根可能走完整個高度。加起來，工作量與 n 成正比，而不是 n log n。`,"O(n) to build a heap from an array. Heap sort begins with exactly this.":`從陣列建立堆積是 O(n)。堆積排序就是從這一步開始的。`},"priority-queues":{"insert it into the heap":`把它插入堆積中`,"take the smallest from the heap":`從堆積中取出最小的`,"return the root, leaving it there":`返回 根，並把它留在原處`,"Who goes next":`下一個是誰`,"Most urgent first":`最緊急的優先`,"An ordinary queue serves whoever has waited longest. A hospital does not work like that: the most urgent case is seen first, whenever it arrived.":`普通佇列服務的是等得最久的人。醫院不是這樣運作的：最緊急的病人先看，不管他什麼時候來的。`,"A <strong>priority queue</strong> does the same. Every item has a priority, and the one that comes out is always the most urgent: here, the smallest number.":`<strong>優先佇列</strong>也是這樣。每個項都有一個優先順序，出來的總是最緊急的那個：這裡是數字最小的。`,"How it is built":`它是怎麼實現的`,"A priority queue says what it does. A heap is the usual way of doing it.":`優先佇列說的是它做什麼。堆積是實現它的常用方法。`,"next to be served":`下一個被服務`,Served:`已服務`,"Waiting is listed in the order they arrived.":`等待中的按到達順序列出。`,"Push: a routine case":`push：一個普通病例`,"A patient with priority 6 arrives. Less urgent than everyone already waiting, so after one comparison with its parent it stays at the bottom.":`一個優先順序為 6 的病人到了。比所有在等的人都不緊急，所以和父節點比較一次後，它留在底部。`,"Nothing else moved.":`其他什麼都沒動。`,"Push: an emergency":`push：一個急診`,"Now a priority 1 arrives, last of all. It starts at the bottom like anyone else, but it is more urgent than its parent, 5, so they swap.":`現在一個優先順序為 1 的病人最後到達。它像其他人一樣從底部開始，但它比父節點 5 更緊急，所以兩者交換。`,"1 < 5: move up":`1 < 5：上移`,"Straight to the front":`直接到最前面`,"And it is more urgent than 3, so they swap too. Two swaps, and the last to arrive is the next to be served.":`它也比 3 更緊急，所以也交換。兩次交換，最後到達的成了下一個被服務的。`,"It did not push past everyone. It only compared itself with the two nodes on its own path to the root.":`它並沒有擠過所有人。它只和自己通往根的路徑上的兩個節點比較過。`,"O(log n): one comparison per level, however many are waiting.":`O(log n)：每層一次比較，不管有多少人在等。`,"<strong>pop()</strong> takes the root: priority 1 is served. The last item, 5, fills the gap and sifts down past 3.":`<strong>pop()</strong> 取走根：優先順序 1 被服務。最後一項 5 填上空位，下沉越過 3。`,"The heap has put the next most urgent case on top by itself. That is 3, which arrived before nearly everyone.":`堆積自己把下一個最緊急的病例放到了頂上。那是 3，它幾乎比所有人來得都早。`,"Why a heap":`為什麼用堆積`,"You could keep the waiting list unsorted: adding is instant, but finding the most urgent means checking everyone. Or keep it sorted: the most urgent is at the front, but every arrival has to be slotted in.":`你可以讓等待列表保持無序：新增是即時的，但找最緊急的要檢查每個人。或者讓它保持有序：最緊急的在最前面，但每次有人到達都得插到正確的位置。`,"A heap is quick at both, because it keeps only as much order as the job needs.":`堆積兩樣都快，因為它只保持這項工作所需的那麼多順序。`,"Operating-system schedulers, event simulations, and the shortest-path search later in this course.":`作業系統排程器、事件模擬，以及本課程後面的最短路徑搜尋。`,"Unsorted list":`無序列表`,"Sorted list":`有序列表`,Heap:`堆積`,"Both jobs matter, so the heap wins.":`兩樣工作都重要，所以堆積勝出。`},"top-k":{"heap ← an empty min-heap":`heap ← 一個空的最小堆積`,"for each x in the stream:":`對每個 流中的 x:`,"if the heap holds fewer than k: insert x":`如果 堆積中少於 k 個: 插入 x`,"else if x > the heap's smallest:":`否則，如果 x > 堆積中最小的:`,"take the smallest out, insert x":`取出最小的，插入 x`,"// otherwise x is not in the top k: drop it":`// 否則 x 不在前 k 名裡：丟掉它`,"return what the heap holds":`返回 堆積中存的東西`,"So far":`目前為止`,"The three biggest":`最大的三個`,"Numbers arrive one at a time: 5, 9, 2, 7, 1, 8… Keep track of the <strong>three biggest</strong> seen so far.":`數字一個一個地到來：5、9、2、7、1、8……記住目前見過的<strong>最大的三個</strong>。`,"Sorting everything works, but it does far too much, and a stream may never end. The trick is to remember only three numbers, in a heap.":`全部排序也行，但做得太多了，而且一個流可能永遠不會結束。訣竅是隻記住三個數，放在一個堆積裡。`,"first to arrive":`最先到達`,Stream:`流`,"Top 3 so far":`目前的前 3 名`,"Smallest of them":`它們中最小的`,"Fill the heap":`填滿堆積`,"The first three go straight in. It is a <strong>min</strong>-heap, so the smallest of the three, 2, sits on top.":`前三個直接放進去。這是一個<strong>最小</strong>堆積，所以三個中最小的 2 在頂上。`,"That seems backwards for finding the biggest. But the one on top is the one most at risk: the weakest of the current top three.":`要找最大的，這看起來是反的。但頂上的那個正是最危險的：當前前三名裡最弱的。`,"To stay in the top three, a newcomer only has to beat the weakest member.":`新來的只要勝過最弱的成員，就能留在前三名裡。`,"weakest of the three":`三個中最弱的`,"A newcomer":`新來的`,"7 arrives. Compare it with the root, and only the root: 7 is bigger than 2.":`7 來了。把它和根比較，只和根比較：7 比 2 大。`,"So 7 belongs in the top three, and 2 no longer does.":`所以 7 屬於前三名，而 2 不再屬於。`,"7 > 2: it is in":`7 > 2：入選`,Replace:`替換`,"2 is taken out and 7 inserted. The heap sorts itself out, and the new weakest member, 5, rises to the top.":`取出 2，插入 7。堆積自己整理好，新的最弱成員 5 升到頂上。`,"The heap never grows past three items, however long the stream is.":`不管流有多長，堆積都不會超過三個項。`,"Not good enough":`不夠好`,"1 arrives. It is smaller than the root, 5, so it is smaller than all three of them.":`1 來了。它比根 5 小，所以比三個都小。`,"One comparison and it is gone. Most of a stream is dismissed this cheaply.":`一次比較，它就被淘汰了。流中的大部分數都是這樣便宜地被打發掉的。`,"1 < 5: dropped":`1 < 5：丟掉`,"The answer so far":`目前的答案`,"8 beats 5, so 5 goes and 8 comes in. The heap now holds 9, 8 and 7: the three biggest of everything seen.":`8 勝過 5，所以 5 出去，8 進來。現在堆積中是 9、8 和 7：目前見過的所有數中最大的三個。`,"Stop the stream at any moment and the answer is ready.":`隨時停下這個流，答案都是現成的。`,"O(n log k) time and only O(k) memory, where sorting needs O(n log n) and all n items.":`O(n log k) 時間，只要 O(k) 記憶體，而排序需要 O(n log n) 並且要存下全部 n 個項。`,"third biggest":`第三大`,"Six numbers seen, three remembered.":`見過六個數，記住了三個。`},"median-of-a-stream":{"if x is no bigger than the top of low: push it on low":`如果 x 不大於 low 的頂部: 把它壓入 low`,"else: push it on high":`否則: 把它壓入 high`,"if one heap has two more than the other:":`如果 一個堆積比另一個多兩個:`,"move its top across":`把它的頂部移過去`,"if the heaps are the same size:":`如果 兩個堆積一樣大:`,"return the average of their two tops":`返回 它們兩個頂部的平均值`,"return the top of the bigger heap":`返回 較大的堆積的頂部`,"The two halves":`兩半`,"The middle of a moving list":`一個不斷變化的列表的中間`,"Numbers arrive one at a time, and after each you may be asked for the <strong>median</strong>: the middle value. Sorting after every arrival is far too slow.":`數字一個一個地到來，每來一個，你都可能被問到<strong>中位數</strong>：中間的值。每來一個就排一次序太慢了。`,"The trick is that the median only depends on the numbers either side of the middle. So keep the numbers in two halves, and watch where they meet.":`訣竅在於中位數只取決於中間兩側的數。所以把數分成兩半存放，看它們在哪裡相接。`,"Lower half":`下半部分`,"biggest on top":`最大的在頂上`,"Upper half":`上半部分`,"smallest on top":`最小的在頂上`,Median:`中位數`,"A heap each side":`每邊一個堆積`,"After 5 and 2: the smaller goes on the left, the bigger on the right. The left side is a <em>max</em>-heap, so its biggest is on top. The right is a <em>min</em>-heap, with its smallest on top.":`5 和 2 之後：小的放左邊，大的放右邊。左邊是<em>最大</em>堆積，所以它最大的在頂上。右邊是<em>最小</em>堆積，最小的在頂上。`,"Those two tops are the numbers nearest the middle. With one each, the median is halfway between: 3.5.":`這兩個頂部就是最接近中間的數。每邊一個時，中位數在它們正中間：3.5。`,"median 3.5":`中位數 3.5`,"Which side does it belong to?":`它屬於哪一邊？`,"8 arrives. It is bigger than the top of the lower half, so it goes on the right, and sinks below 5.":`8 來了。它比下半部分的頂部大，所以放到右邊，沉到 5 下面。`,"The right side now has one more. The median is the top of the bigger side: 5.":`右邊現在多一個。中位數就是較大那一邊的頂部：5。`,"median 5":`中位數 5`,"Even again":`又一樣多了`,"1 arrives and belongs on the left, under 2. Two each: the median is the average of the tops again, 3.5.":`1 來了，屬於左邊，在 2 下面。每邊兩個：中位數又是兩個頂部的平均值，3.5。`,Lopsided:`一邊倒`,"9 and then 7 both belong on the right. That would leave four on the right against two on the left: the halves are no longer halves.":`9 和 7 都屬於右邊。那樣右邊就有四個，左邊只有兩個：兩半不再是兩半了。`,"7 is still to come.":`7 還沒來。`,"Pass one across":`移一個過去`,Rebalance:`再平衡`,"So when 7 goes in on the right, the right’s top, 5, moves over to the left. It is the smallest of the upper half, which makes it the biggest of the lower.":`所以當 7 放進右邊時，右邊的頂部 5 移到左邊。它是上半部分中最小的，所以它就成了下半部分中最大的。`,"Three each. The tops are 5 and 7, and the median is 6.":`每邊三個。頂部是 5 和 7，中位數是 6。`,"O(log n) to add a number, O(1) to read the median.":`新增一個數 O(log n)，讀取中位數 O(1)。`,"median 6":`中位數 6`},"heap-sort":{"arrange a as a max-heap":`把 a 整理成一個最大堆積`,"for end from the last cell down to the second:":`對於 end 從最後一個格子倒著到第二個:`,"swap a[0] with a[end]      // the biggest goes to the end":`交換 a[0] 和 a[end]      // 最大的去末尾`,"sift a[0] down, ignoring cells from end onwards":`讓 a[0] 下沉，忽略從 end 開始的格子`,"In the array":`在陣列中`,"A heap knows its biggest":`堆積知道它最大的是誰`,"This is a <strong>max-heap</strong>: every parent is bigger than its children, so the biggest value is at the root.":`這是一個<strong>最大堆積</strong>：每個父節點都比它的孩子大，所以最大的值在根上。`,"Sorting with it is simple to state. Take the biggest, then the biggest of what is left, and so on. The clever part is where the taken values are kept.":`用它排序，說起來很簡單。取出最大的，再取出剩下的裡面最大的，依此類推。巧妙之處在於取出的值存放在哪裡。`,"the biggest":`最大的`,"Still a heap":`仍是堆積`,Sorted:`已排序`,"Swap it to the end":`把它換到末尾`,"Swap the root with the last item of the heap. 9 is now in the last cell of the array, which is exactly where the biggest value belongs.":`把根和堆積的最後一項交換。9 現在在陣列的最後一個格子裡，正是最大的值該在的地方。`,"Fence that cell off. The heap is one smaller, and its root is wrong.":`把那個格子隔開。堆積少了一個，而它的根不對了。`,"Repair the heap":`修復堆積`,"Sift the new root down, as when taking from any heap: 4 swaps with its bigger child, 8. The fenced cell is not looked at.":`讓新的根下沉，和從任何堆積中取值時一樣：4 和它較大的孩子 8 交換。隔開的格子不看。`,"The biggest of what remains is on top again.":`剩下的裡面最大的又在頂上了。`,"Swap 8 to the end of the heap, beside 9, and fence it off. Sift 5 down past 7.":`把 8 換到堆積的末尾，在 9 旁邊，把它隔開。讓 5 下沉越過 7。`,"The sorted part grows from the back of the array as the heap shrinks from the front.":`隨著堆積從前面縮小，已排序的部分從陣列後面增長。`,"7 goes to the end of the heap and is fenced off. 3, now on top, sifts down past 5.":`7 去到堆積的末尾並被隔開。現在在頂上的 3 下沉越過 5。`,"Half the array is sorted, and the heap is down to three.":`陣列排好了一半，堆積只剩三個。`,"Until the heap is gone":`直到堆積沒了`,"Two more rounds and nothing is left in the heap. Read the tree level by level, which is the order of the array: 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9.":`再來兩輪，堆積裡就什麼都不剩了。一層一層地讀這棵樹，也就是陣列的順序：3、4、5、7、8、9。`,"No second array was needed. The heap and the sorted part shared the one array throughout.":`不需要第二個陣列。堆積和已排序的部分始終共用同一個陣列。`,"O(n log n) always, with O(1) extra memory. It does not keep equal items in their original order.":`總是 O(n log n)，額外記憶體 O(1)。它不會讓相等的項保持原來的順序。`},"graph-representation":{"How it is stored":`它是怎麼儲存的`,"Things…":`一些東西……`,"A list puts things in a line. A tree puts them in a hierarchy. Most of the world is neither: towns joined by roads, people who know each other, pages that link to pages.":`列表把東西排成一行。樹把它們排成層級。世界上大多數東西兩者都不是：用道路相連的城鎮、互相認識的人、互相連結的網頁。`,"A <strong>graph</strong> is how to hold that. It starts with a set of things, called <strong>nodes</strong> (or vertices).":`<strong>圖</strong>就是用來存放這些的。它從一組東西開始，這些東西叫<strong>節點</strong>（或頂點）。`,"no neighbours":`沒有鄰居`,"Six nodes, nothing joining them yet.":`六個節點，還沒有任何連線。`,"…and the links between them":`……以及它們之間的連線`,"Then come the <strong>edges</strong>: each one joins two nodes. That is all a graph is. There is no first node, no root, no order.":`然後是<strong>邊</strong>：每條邊連線兩個節點。圖就是這麼簡單。沒有第一個節點，沒有根，也沒有順序。`,"A linked list is a graph where every node has one way on. A tree is a graph with no loops. Graphs are the general case.":`連結串列是每個節點只有一條出路的圖。樹是沒有環的圖。圖是一般情況。`,"Each row lists a node’s neighbours.":`每一行列出一個節點的鄰居。`,"Two nodes joined by an edge are <strong>neighbours</strong>. B has three: A, D and E.":`由一條邊相連的兩個節點互為<strong>鄰居</strong>。B 有三個：A、D 和 E。`,"Nearly every graph algorithm comes down to one move, repeated: “for each neighbour of this node…”. So the way a graph is stored has to make that move quick.":`幾乎每個圖演算法都歸結為一個反覆進行的動作：「對這個節點的每個鄰居……」。所以圖的儲存方式必須讓這個動作很快。`,"An adjacency list":`鄰接表`,"The usual way: for every node, keep a list of its neighbours. To visit E’s neighbours, go to E’s list and read it: B, F.":`常用的方法：為每個節點儲存一個鄰居列表。要訪問 E 的鄰居，就去 E 的列表讀：B、F。`,"It takes space for each node and each edge and nothing more. For graphs where most pairs are <em>not</em> joined, which is almost all real ones, this is what you want.":`它只為每個節點和每條邊佔用空間，別無其他。對於大多數節點對<em>沒有</em>相連的圖，也就是幾乎所有真實的圖，這正是你想要的。`,"Space O(V + E). Listing a node’s neighbours takes as long as it has neighbours.":`空間 O(V + E)。列出一個節點的鄰居，所需時間和它的鄰居數一樣多。`,"An adjacency matrix":`鄰接矩陣`,"The other way: a grid with a row and a column for every node, and a 1 wherever two are joined. “Is C joined to F?” is one look: row C, column F.":`另一種方法：一個網格，每個節點佔一行一列，兩個節點相連的地方寫 1。「C 和 F 相連嗎？」看一眼就知道：C 行，F 列。`,"That answer is instant. But the grid has a cell for every possible pair, used or not, and finding a node’s neighbours means reading its whole row.":`這個答案是即時的。但網格為每一對可能的節點都留了一個格子，不管用沒用到，而且找一個節點的鄰居要讀完它整行。`,"Space O(V²). Good for small or dense graphs; wasteful for big sparse ones.":`空間 O(V²)。適合小的或稠密的圖；對大的稀疏圖很浪費。`,"Columns run A to F, like the rows.":`列和行一樣，從 A 到 F。`,"Direction and weight":`方向與權重`,Variations:`變體`,"Two things can be added to an edge. A <strong>weight</strong>: a number for what it costs to use, such as a distance or a time. And a <strong>direction</strong>: a one-way street, or “follows” on a social network.":`一條邊可以多加兩樣東西。<strong>權重</strong>：表示使用它的代價的數字，比如距離或時間。還有<strong>方向</strong>：一條單行道，或者社交網路上的「關注」。`,"Either store is easily extended. A list keeps the weight beside each neighbour; a matrix puts the weight where the 1 was.":`兩種儲存方式都很容易擴充套件。鄰接表在每個鄰居旁邊存上權重；鄰接矩陣把權重寫在原來寫 1 的地方。`,"Each neighbour, with the weight of the edge to it.":`每個鄰居，以及通往它的邊的權重。`},"breadth-first-search":{"mark start as seen, put it in a queue":`把 start 標記為已見，放進一個佇列`,"node ← take the front of the queue":`node ← 取出隊首`,"mark it as seen":`把它標記為已見`,"put it at the back of the queue":`把它放到隊尾`,"Waiting their turn":`等著輪到它們`,"Nearest first":`最近的優先`,"Starting from A, visit every node that can be reached. A graph has no order of its own, so the search has to choose one.":`從 A 出發，訪問所有能到達的節點。圖本身沒有順序，所以搜尋必須自己選一個。`,"<strong>Breadth-first search</strong> goes outwards in rings: everything one edge away, then everything two away, and so on. It is how a ripple spreads.":`<strong>廣度優先搜尋</strong>一圈一圈地向外擴充套件：先是一條邊之外的一切，然後是兩條邊之外的一切，依此類推。就像漣漪擴散那樣。`,Queue:`佇列`,"The first ring":`第一圈`,"A is at distance 0. Look at each of its neighbours: B and C have not been seen, so mark them and put them in a <strong>queue</strong>.":`A 的距離是 0。看它的每個鄰居：B 和 C 還沒見過，所以標記它們，並放進一個<strong>佇列</strong>。`,"The number on a node is how many edges it is from A.":`節點上的數字是它離 A 有幾條邊。`,"The queue keeps the order":`佇列保持順序`,"B is at the front, so B goes next. Its unseen neighbours, D and E, are two edges from A. They join the <em>back</em> of the queue, behind C.":`B 在隊首，所以下一個是 B。它沒見過的鄰居 D 和 E，離 A 有兩條邊。它們排到佇列的<em>末尾</em>，在 C 後面。`,"Because it is a queue, everything at distance 1 is dealt with before anything at distance 2.":`因為這是佇列，所有距離為 1 的都會在距離為 2 的之前處理完。`,"Seen means skip":`見過就跳過`,"C’s turn. One neighbour, A, is already seen, so it is skipped. The other, F, is new.":`輪到 C。一個鄰居 A 已經見過，所以跳過。另一個 F 是新的。`,"Marking nodes as seen is what stops the search going round in circles, and what makes sure each node is handled once.":`把節點標記為已見，才讓搜尋不會繞圈子，並且保證每個節點只處理一次。`,"Fewest edges":`邊數最少`,"D, E and F have no unseen neighbours, so the queue empties and the search is over. The edge between E and F was never needed.":`D、E 和 F 都沒有沒見過的鄰居，所以佇列清空，搜尋結束。E 和 F 之間的邊根本沒用上。`,"Every node now carries its distance from A, and the coloured edges are the shortest routes. In a graph without weights, breadth-first search <em>is</em> the shortest-path algorithm.":`現在每個節點都帶著它離 A 的距離，著色的邊就是最短的路線。在沒有權重的圖裡，廣度優先搜尋<em>就是</em>最短路徑演算法。`,"O(V + E): each node enters the queue once, and each edge is looked at twice.":`O(V + E)：每個節點進佇列一次，每條邊看兩次。`,"2 edges from A":`離 A 兩條邊`,"Visited in order of distance.":`按距離順序訪問。`},"depth-first-search":{"mark node as seen":`把 node 標記為已見`,"dfs(neighbour)        // go deeper":`dfs(neighbour)        // 走得更深`,"// nothing left here: go back":`// 這裡什麼都不剩了：往回走`,"Where it has been":`它走過的地方`,"As far as it goes":`能走多遠走多遠`,"Breadth-first search spreads out evenly. <strong>Depth-first search</strong> does the opposite: pick a way and follow it as far as it goes, and only come back when there is nowhere new to go.":`廣度優先搜尋均勻地鋪開。<strong>深度優先搜尋</strong>正好相反：選一條路一直走到底，只有在沒有新地方可去時才回來。`,"It is how you would explore a maze with a ball of string.":`就像你拿著一團線去探索迷宮。`,"Path from the start":`從起點出發的路徑`,"the stack":`堆疊`,"Go deep":`往深處走`,"From A take the first unseen neighbour, B. Do not look at A’s other neighbour yet. From B take its first unseen neighbour, D.":`從 A 走向第一個沒見過的鄰居 B。先不看 A 的另一個鄰居。從 B 走向它第一個沒見過的鄰居 D。`,"The numbers are the order nodes were first reached in.":`數字是各節點第一次被到達的順序。`,"Dead end: back up":`死路：退回`,"D has no unseen neighbours, so it is finished. Go <strong>back</strong> the way you came, to B, and try B’s next neighbour: E.":`D 沒有沒見過的鄰居，所以它完成了。沿著來路<strong>退回</strong> B，試試 B 的下一個鄰居：E。`,"Going back is the string being wound in. In code it is a function returning, or a stack being popped.":`往回走就是收線。在程式碼裡，就是函式返回，或者堆疊彈出。`,"Deep again":`再往深處走`,"From E on to F, and from F on to C. Each time the search just takes the next step it can.":`從 E 到 F，再從 F 到 C。每次搜尋都只是走它能走的下一步。`,"Notice C: it is right next to A, and it is the last node reached.":`注意 C：它就在 A 旁邊，卻是最後到達的節點。`,Unwind:`回退`,"C’s only other neighbour is A, already seen. So back to F, to E, to B, to A, each with nothing new to offer.":`C 唯一的另一個鄰居是 A，已經見過了。所以退回 F、E、B、A，每一個都沒有新東西了。`,"Back at the start with nothing left: every node has been visited once.":`回到起點，什麼都不剩：每個節點都被訪問了一次。`,"O(V + E), the same as breadth-first. Only the order differs.":`O(V + E)，和廣度優先一樣。只是順序不同。`,"Finished deepest first.":`最深的最先完成。`,"A way, not the best way":`一條路，而不是最好的路`,"Depth-first search reached C through B, E and F: four edges, when C is one edge from A. It finds <em>a</em> route, not the shortest one.":`深度優先搜尋經過 B、E 和 F 才到達 C：四條邊，而 C 離 A 只有一條邊。它找到的是<em>一條</em>路線，而不是最短的那條。`,"What it is good at is questions about structure: is there any way through, is there a loop, what has to come before what. And it needs only a stack, which recursion gives for free.":`它擅長的是關於結構的問題：有沒有路能透過、有沒有環、什麼必須在什麼之前。而且它只需要一個堆疊，遞迴免費就提供了。`,"Nearest or fewest steps: breadth-first. Everything, in some order, or anything about loops: depth-first.":`最近的或步數最少：廣度優先。全部訪問一遍，或者任何關於環的問題：深度優先。`,"4 edges, not 1":`4 條邊，而不是 1 條`},"connected-components":{"for each node:":`對每個 節點:`,"if it has no label yet:":`如果 它還沒有標籤:`,"spread out from it, labelling":`從它向外擴充套件，把`,"everything reached with count":`到達的一切都標記為 count`,"The pieces":`各個部分`,"How many pieces?":`有幾個部分？`,"A graph need not be all in one piece. This one clearly is not, but a program cannot see that at a glance: it has only a list of edges.":`圖不一定是連成一整塊的。這個圖顯然不是，但程式沒法一眼看出來：它只有一張邊的列表。`,"Each piece, in which every node can reach every other, is a <strong>connected component</strong>.":`每個部分中，每個節點都能到達其他所有節點，這樣的部分叫作<strong>連通分量</strong>。`,"Groups found":`已找到的組`,"Spread from any node":`從任意節點擴充套件`,"Pick a node that has no label, A, and search outwards from it: breadth-first or depth-first, either will do. Everything reached gets the label 1.":`選一個沒有標籤的節點 A，從它向外搜尋：廣度優先或深度優先都行。到達的一切都得到標籤 1。`,"The search stops by itself when the piece runs out.":`這個部分走完時，搜尋會自己停下。`,"Find the next unlabelled one":`找下一個沒有標籤的`,"Carry on down the list of nodes. B and C are already labelled, so skip them. D is not: it starts piece 2, and the search from it finds E.":`沿著節點列表繼續往下。B 和 C 已經有標籤了，跳過。D 沒有：它開始第 2 部分，從它出發的搜尋找到了 E。`,"A piece of one":`只有一個的部分`,"F has no label and no edges. It is a component all by itself: piece 3.":`F 沒有標籤，也沒有邊。它自己就是一個連通分量：第 3 部分。`,"on its own":`獨自一個`,"The paint bucket":`油漆桶`,"Three pieces. Every node was labelled once and every edge looked at twice.":`三個部分。每個節點被標記一次，每條邊被看兩次。`,"On a grid, where a cell’s neighbours are the cells beside it, this is <strong>flood fill</strong>: the paint-bucket tool, counting islands on a map, finding the rooms in a floor plan.":`在網格上，一個格子的鄰居就是它旁邊的格子，這就是<strong>泛洪填充</strong>：油漆桶工具、數地圖上的島嶼、找出平面圖裡的房間。`,"O(V + E). Union-find answers the same question when edges arrive one at a time.":`O(V + E)。當邊一條一條地到來時，並查集回答的是同一個問題。`},"cycle-detection":{"put node on the path":`把 node 放到路徑上`,"for each arrow node → next:":`對每個 箭頭 node → next:`,"if next is on the path: return yes":`如果 next 在路徑上: 返回 是`,"if next is new and has_cycle(next): return yes":`如果 next 是新的且 has_cycle(next): 返回 是`,"take node off the path, mark it finished":`把 node 從路徑上拿下，標記為已完成`,"Going round in circles":`繞圈子`,"If job B waits for D, D waits for C, and C waits for B, none of them can ever start. A loop like that is a <strong>cycle</strong>.":`如果任務 B 等 D，D 等 C，而 C 又等 B，它們誰都永遠開始不了。這樣的迴圈叫作<strong>環</strong>。`,"A build system has to refuse it, a spreadsheet has to report a circular reference, and a topological sort has no answer. So: does this graph have one?":`構建系統必須拒絕它，電子表格必須報告迴圈引用，拓撲排序也沒有答案。所以：這個圖裡有環嗎？`,"On the path":`在路徑上`,Cycle:`環`,"Remember the way you came":`記住你來的路`,"Search depth-first from A, and keep a note of the <strong>path</strong>: the nodes between the start and where you are standing now.":`從 A 開始深度優先搜尋，並記下<strong>路徑</strong>：起點和你現在所站位置之間的節點。`,"A, then B, then C. All three are on the path.":`A，然後 B，然後 C。三個都在路徑上。`,"A dead end is fine":`死路沒關係`,"From C, try E. It has no arrows out, so there is nothing more to find beyond it. Mark it finished and step back to C.":`從 C 試試 E。它沒有出去的箭頭，所以在它後面再也找不到什麼了。把它標記為已完成，退回 C。`,"E comes off the path. A finished node can never be part of a loop through where you are now.":`E 從路徑上拿下。一個已完成的節點永遠不可能是經過你當前位置的環的一部分。`,finished:`已完成`,"An arrow back onto the path":`一個指回路徑上的箭頭`,"C’s other arrow goes to D, and D’s arrow goes to B. But B is <em>on the path</em>: it is one of the nodes that led here.":`C 的另一個箭頭指向 D，而 D 的箭頭指向 B。但 B <em>在路徑上</em>：它是通向這裡的節點之一。`,"So there is a way from B to D, and now an arrow from D back to B. That is a cycle: B, C, D, and round again.":`所以從 B 有路到 D，現在又有一個從 D 指回 B 的箭頭。這就是一個環：B、C、D，再繞回來。`,"already on the path":`已經在路徑上`,"Visited is not enough":`只看「訪問過」還不夠`,"The rule needs three kinds of node: new, on the path, and finished. Meeting a finished node again is harmless: two routes to the same place, like a diamond. Only an arrow to a node still on the path closes a loop.":`這條規則需要三種節點：新的、在路徑上的、已完成的。再次遇到已完成的節點是無害的：兩條路通向同一個地方，就像菱形那樣。只有指向仍在路徑上的節點的箭頭，才會閉合成環。`,"With no arrows, just plain edges, it is simpler: any visited node other than the one you just came from means a cycle.":`如果沒有箭頭，只有普通的邊，就更簡單了：除了你剛剛來的那個節點，遇到任何訪問過的節點都意味著有環。`,"O(V + E): one depth-first search.":`O(V + E)：一次深度優先搜尋。`},"topological-sort":{"count the arrows coming in to each node":`數出指向每個節點的箭頭數`,"ready ← every node with none":`ready ← 所有沒有箭頭指向的節點`,"while ready is not empty:":`當 ready 不為空:`,"take a node from ready, add it to the order":`從 ready 中取出一個節點，把它加到順序裡`,"for each node it points at:":`對每個 它指向的節點:`,"one fewer arrow comes in to that node":`指向那個節點的箭頭少一個`,"if none are left: add it to ready":`如果 一個都不剩了: 把它加進 ready`,"if any node was never taken: there is a loop":`如果 有節點從沒被取出: 就存在一個環`,"The order":`順序`,"What must come first":`什麼必須先做`,"Six jobs, and some depend on others: an arrow from A to C means A has to be finished before C can start. Courses with prerequisites, steps in a build, getting dressed.":`六項任務，有些依賴於別的：從 A 指向 C 的箭頭表示 A 必須完成後 C 才能開始。有先修要求的課程、構建中的步驟、穿衣服。`,"A <strong>topological order</strong> is a way to line the jobs up so that every arrow points forwards. No job comes before something it depends on.":`<strong>拓撲順序</strong>是一種排列任務的方式，讓每個箭頭都指向前方。沒有任務會排在它所依賴的東西之前。`,"Order so far":`目前的順序`,"Ready now":`現在可以做`,"Count what each waits for":`數一數每個在等什麼`,"For every job, count the arrows coming <em>in</em>: how many things it is still waiting for.":`對每項任務，數出指<em>向</em>它的箭頭：它還在等幾件事。`,"A and B are waiting for nothing. They can be done right away.":`A 和 B 什麼都不等。它們馬上就可以做。`,"Do one that is ready":`做一個準備好的`,"Do A. Everything A pointed at now has one thing fewer to wait for: C drops from 2 to 1.":`做 A。A 指向的一切現在都少等一件事：C 從 2 降到 1。`,"C is still waiting for B, so it is not ready yet.":`C 還在等 B，所以它還沒準備好。`,"Finishing frees others":`完成一項會釋放別的`,"Do B. Its arrows go to C and D, and both drop to zero.":`做 B。它的箭頭指向 C 和 D，兩個都降到了零。`,"Two more jobs have just become ready. Nothing was searched for: finishing B is what revealed them.":`又有兩項任務剛剛準備好。沒有搜尋任何東西：是完成 B 讓它們顯現出來的。`,"Keep going":`繼續`,"Do C, which frees E. Do D, which leaves F waiting for one thing. Do E, and F is free.":`做 C，它釋放了 E。做 D，F 還剩一件事要等。做 E，F 就自由了。`,"Whenever more than one job is ready, either may go first. There is usually more than one valid order.":`每當有不止一項任務準備好時，哪個先做都行。有效的順序通常不止一種。`,"Every arrow points forwards":`每個箭頭都指向前方`,"F is last. The order is A, B, C, D, E, F, and every dependency is respected.":`F 最後。順序是 A、B、C、D、E、F，每個依賴關係都被遵守了。`,"If jobs were left over with nothing ready, they would be waiting on each other in a circle: a loop, and no order exists. So this is also how dependency loops are detected.":`如果還剩下任務，卻沒有一個準備好，它們就是在互相繞圈等待：一個環，不存在任何順序。所以這也是檢測依賴環的方法。`,"O(V + E): every job is taken once and every arrow is counted off once.":`O(V + E)：每項任務取出一次，每個箭頭扣減一次。`,"Only works on a graph with no loops.":`只適用於沒有環的圖。`},"strongly-connected-components":{"order ← the nodes, as a depth-first search":`order ← 按深度優先搜尋完成的順序`,"finishes with them":`排列的節點`,"for each node, last finished first:":`對每個 節點，最後完成的優先:`,"if it has no group yet:":`如果 它還沒有組:`,"walk the arrows backwards from it,":`從它出發逆著箭頭走，`,"labelling every unlabelled node reached":`把到達的每個未標記節點都標記上`,"There, but not back":`能去，但回不來`,"With arrows, getting somewhere and getting back are different questions. From A you can reach F. From F you cannot reach anything.":`有了箭頭，到達某處和回來就是不同的問題了。從 A 你能到達 F。從 F 你哪裡都到不了。`,"Two nodes are <strong>strongly connected</strong> when each can reach the other. The question is how the graph falls apart into groups like that.":`當兩個節點能互相到達時，它們就是<strong>強連通</strong>的。問題是圖如何分裂成這樣的組。`,"Finished in this order":`按這個順序完成`,"A loop holds a group together":`環把一組連在一起`,"A points to B, B to C, and C back to A. Start at any of the three and you can get to the other two, and home again.":`A 指向 B，B 指向 C，C 又指回 A。從三個中的任何一個出發，你都能到達另外兩個，再回家。`,"These three form one <strong>strongly connected component</strong>.":`這三個構成一個<strong>強連通分量</strong>。`,"A one-way road divides":`一條單行道把它們分開`,"C has a road to D, but nothing comes back from D’s side. So D is not in the first group.":`C 有一條路通向 D，但從 D 那邊沒有路回來。所以 D 不在第一組裡。`,"D and E point at each other: a group of two. F can be reached but leads nowhere: a group of one. Three components, joined by one-way roads.":`D 和 E 互相指向：一個兩個節點的組。F 能被到達，但哪裡都去不了：一個只有一個節點的組。三個分量，由單行道連線。`,"no way back to C":`沒有回 C 的路`,"Pass one: go as deep as you can":`第一遍：儘可能往深處走`,"That was by eye. A program does it with two depth-first searches. The first is an ordinary one: from A, follow arrows as far as they go.":`剛才是用眼睛看的。程式用兩次深度優先搜尋來做。第一次是普通的：從 A 出發，沿著箭頭能走多遠走多遠。`,"A, B, C, D, E, F. At F there is nowhere left to go.":`A、B、C、D、E、F。到了 F 就無處可去了。`,"Number them on the way out":`在出來的路上編號`,"The search backs out the way it came. Number each node as it is <em>finished</em>: F first, then E, D, C, B, and A last.":`搜尋沿著來路退出。在每個節點<em>完成</em>時給它編號：F 最先，然後是 E、D、C、B，A 最後。`,"The node finished last is always in a group that no other group leads into. That is the fact the second pass relies on.":`最後完成的節點，總是在一個沒有其他組通向它的組裡。第二遍依靠的就是這個事實。`,"Pass two: walk the arrows backwards":`第二遍：逆著箭頭走`,"Take the highest number, A, and walk <em>against</em> the arrows. That reaches C, then B. Nothing outside leads into this group, so the walk cannot leak out of it: group 1.":`取編號最大的 A，<em>逆著</em>箭頭走。這會到達 C，然後是 B。外面沒有東西通向這個組，所以這次行走不會漏出去：第 1 組。`,"The highest number left is D. Backwards from D reaches E, and C is already taken: group 2. Then F by itself: group 3.":`剩下編號最大的是 D。從 D 逆著走到達 E，而 C 已經被佔了：第 2 組。然後 F 自己：第 3 組。`,"A map of the groups":`組的地圖`,"Shrink each group to a single dot and what is left has no loops at all: group 1 leads to group 2, which leads to group 3. That can be put in topological order.":`把每個組縮成一個點，剩下的部分完全沒有環：第 1 組通向第 2 組，第 2 組通向第 3 組。這可以排成拓撲順序。`,"This is how a build tool finds modules that depend on each other in a circle, and how a compiler finds functions that call each other.":`構建工具就是這樣找出互相迴圈依賴的模組的，編譯器也是這樣找出互相呼叫的函式的。`,"O(V + E): two depth-first searches. This two-pass method is Kosaraju’s algorithm.":`O(V + E)：兩次深度優先搜尋。這種兩遍的方法叫 Kosaraju 演算法。`},"shortest-paths":{"while some node is not settled:":`當 還有節點沒有確定:`,"node ← the nearest unsettled node":`node ← 最近的未確定節點`,"settle it":`確定它`,"for each neighbour, by an edge w:":`對每個 鄰居，經過一條權重為 w 的邊:`,"if best[node] + w < best[neighbour]:":`如果 best[node] + w < best[neighbour]:`,"Not all edges are equal":`不是所有邊都一樣`,"When edges have weights, the fewest edges is no longer the shortest way. A to B direct costs 4. A to C to B is two edges, and costs 3.":`邊有權重時，邊數最少就不再是最短的路了。從 A 直達 B 花費 4。A 經 C 到 B 是兩條邊，花費 3。`,"<strong>Dijkstra’s algorithm</strong> finds the cheapest route from one node to every other. It is breadth-first search that pays attention to cost.":`<strong>Dijkstra 演算法</strong>找出從一個節點到其他每個節點的最便宜路線。它就是關注代價的廣度優先搜尋。`,"Best guesses":`最佳估計`,"Give every node a best known distance from A. A itself is 0. Nothing else has been reached, so everything else starts at infinity.":`給每個節點一個已知離 A 最近的距離。A 自己是 0。其他還沒到達過，所以其餘的一開始都是無窮大。`,"These are guesses that can only get better. The work is improving them until they are right.":`這些估計只會越來越好。工作就是改進它們，直到它們正確為止。`,"Settle the nearest":`確定最近的`,"The unsettled node with the smallest distance is A, at 0. Nothing can be closer, so 0 is final: A is <strong>settled</strong>.":`距離最小的未確定節點是 A，為 0。不可能有更近的了，所以 0 是最終結果：A <strong>確定</strong>了。`,"Now try each edge out of A. B can be reached for 4 and C for 1, both better than infinity.":`現在試試 A 出去的每條邊。B 花 4 就能到達，C 花 1，都比無窮大好。`,settled:`已確定`,"A better way round":`繞一下更好`,"The nearest unsettled node is now C, at 1, so settle it. From C, B costs 1 + 2 = 3. That beats the 4 it had, so B’s guess improves and its route changes.":`現在最近的未確定節點是 C，為 1，所以確定它。從 C 出發，B 的花費是 1 + 2 = 3。這比原來的 4 好，所以 B 的估計改進了，它的路線也變了。`,"E is reached for the first time: 1 + 7 = 8.":`E 第一次被到達：1 + 7 = 8。`,"Why settle the nearest":`為什麼確定最近的`,"Every other route to it would go through something farther away first, so none can be shorter.":`通往它的其他任何路線都要先經過更遠的地方，所以沒有一條能更短。`,"Outwards by cost":`按代價向外擴充套件`,"B is next, at 3. Through B, D can be reached for 3 + 3 = 6.":`下一個是 B，為 3。經過 B，D 花 3 + 3 = 6 就能到達。`,"The settled nodes spread outwards from A in order of distance: 0, 1, 3. Next will be whichever of D and E is closer.":`已確定的節點按距離順序從 A 向外擴充套件：0、1、3。下一個會是 D 和 E 中更近的那個。`,"Every distance final":`每個距離都是最終的`,"D settles at 6, and through it E improves once more: 6 + 1 = 7, beating the direct road from C. E settles last.":`D 在 6 確定，經過它，E 又改進了一次：6 + 1 = 7，勝過了從 C 直達的路。E 最後確定。`,"The coloured edges are the cheapest route to every town. The best way to E uses four roads, and two of the six roads are not used at all.":`著色的邊是通往每個城鎮最便宜的路線。去 E 的最好路線用了四條路，而六條路中有兩條根本沒用上。`,"O((V + E) log V) with a priority queue to find the nearest. Weights must not be negative.":`用優先佇列找最近的節點，是 O((V + E) log V)。權重不能是負數。`,"Settled nearest first.":`最近的最先確定。`},"bellman-ford":{"repeat (number of nodes − 1) times:":`重複 (節點數 − 1) 次:`,"for each edge u → v, of weight w:":`對每個 權重為 w 的邊 u → v:`,"if best[u] + w < best[v]:":`如果 best[u] + w < best[v]:`,"if any edge could still improve something:":`如果 還有邊能改進什麼:`,"there is a negative cycle":`就存在一個負環`,"A road that pays you":`一條倒貼錢的路`,"Dijkstra’s algorithm settles the nearest node and never looks at it again. Here it would settle B at 4, by the direct road.":`Dijkstra 演算法確定了最近的節點，就再也不看它了。在這裡，它會透過直達的路把 B 確定為 4。`,"But C to B costs −3. Going round by C costs 5 − 3 = 2. With a negative edge, a longer way round can turn out cheaper, and settling early is wrong.":`但 C 到 B 的花費是 −3。繞道 C 的花費是 5 − 3 = 2。有了負權邊，繞遠的路可能反而更便宜，過早確定就錯了。`,"4, or 2?":`4，還是 2？`,Pass:`輪`,"Settle nothing":`什麼都不確定`,"<strong>Bellman–Ford</strong> makes no early decisions. Start the same way: A is 0, everything else infinity.":`<strong>Bellman–Ford</strong> 不做任何過早的決定。開始的方式一樣：A 是 0，其他都是無窮大。`,"Then go through <em>every edge</em>, asking one question each time: does this edge give its far end a better distance? And do that whole pass again and again.":`然後過一遍<em>每一條邊</em>，每次只問一個問題：這條邊能讓它的另一端得到更好的距離嗎？然後把這一整輪一遍又一遍地重複。`,"Pass one":`第一輪`,"B to D and C to B do nothing yet: B and C are still at infinity. A to B gives B a distance of 4. A to C gives C 5.":`B 到 D 和 C 到 B 還什麼都做不了：B 和 C 還是無窮大。A 到 B 給了 B 距離 4。A 到 C 給了 C 距離 5。`,"One pass, and everything one edge from A is known.":`一輪下來，離 A 一條邊的一切都知道了。`,"Pass two":`第二輪`,"B to D: 4 + 2 gives D a distance of 6. Then C to B: 5 − 3 = 2, which beats 4. B improves.":`B 到 D：4 + 2 給了 D 距離 6。然後 C 到 B：5 − 3 = 2，勝過了 4。B 改進了。`,"D’s 6 was worked out from B’s old distance, so it is now out of date. Nobody goes back to fix it. The next pass will.":`D 的 6 是根據 B 的舊距離算出來的，所以現在過時了。沒有人回去修正它。下一輪會修正。`,"Pass three":`第三輪`,"B to D again: 2 + 2 = 4, better than 6. Nothing else changes.":`再次 B 到 D：2 + 2 = 4，比 6 好。其他都沒變。`,"Each pass pushes correct distances one edge further out. The cheapest way to D is three edges long, so it took three passes.":`每一輪都把正確的距離再往外推一條邊。去 D 最便宜的路有三條邊長，所以要三輪。`,"Slow, but never fooled":`慢，但從不上當`,"A cheapest route never needs more than (nodes − 1) edges, so that many passes is always enough.":`最便宜的路線永遠不需要超過 (節點數 − 1) 條邊，所以這麼多輪總是夠的。`,"Run one extra pass. If something <em>still</em> improves, there is a loop whose total is negative: go round it for ever and the cost keeps falling. Bellman–Ford is how you find that out.":`再多跑一輪。如果<em>仍然</em>有東西改進，就存在一個總和為負的環：永遠繞著它走，代價就會一直下降。Bellman–Ford 就是用來發現這一點的。`,"O(V × E). Dijkstra is much faster, so use this only when an edge can be negative.":`O(V × E)。Dijkstra 快得多，所以只在邊可能為負時才用這個。`},"floyd-warshall":{"dist[i][j] ← the road from i to j, or ∞":`dist[i][j] ← 從 i 到 j 的路，或者 ∞`,"for each node k:              // one more stopover allowed":`對每個 節點 k:              // 多允許一箇中轉站`,"for each node i:":`對每個 節點 i:`,"for each node j:":`對每個 節點 j:`,"if dist[i][k] + dist[k][j] < dist[i][j]:":`如果 dist[i][k] + dist[k][j] < dist[i][j]:`,"Every pair at once":`一次求出每一對`,"Dijkstra and Bellman–Ford give the distances from <em>one</em> start. A route planner wants the whole table: from every town to every other.":`Dijkstra 和 Bellman–Ford 給出的是從<em>一個</em>起點出發的距離。路線規劃器想要整張表：從每個城鎮到其他每個城鎮。`,"Start with what is certain: the direct roads. Each row is where a journey starts and each column where it ends. No road means infinity.":`先從確定的東西開始：直達的路。每一行是旅程的起點，每一列是終點。沒有路就是無窮大。`,"A to B: 3":`A 到 B：3`,Roads:`道路`,"Stopovers allowed":`允許的中轉站`,"Pairs with a route":`有路線的點對`,"Allow one stopover":`允許一箇中轉站`,"Now let journeys pass through A. For each pair, compare what is in the table with going to A and on from there.":`現在讓旅程可以經過 A。對每一對，比較表裡的值和先到 A 再從那裡出發的路線。`,"Only D has a road into A. D to A is 2 and A to B is 3, so D to B is 5. The same way, D to C is 2 + 7 = 9.":`只有 D 有路通向 A。D 到 A 是 2，A 到 B 是 3，所以 D 到 B 是 5。同樣地，D 到 C 是 2 + 7 = 9。`,"Then a second":`然後是第二個`,"Allow B as well. A to C was 7 by the direct road. Through B it is 3 + 1 = 4, so the 7 is replaced.":`再允許 B。A 到 C 走直達的路是 7。經過 B 是 3 + 1 = 4，所以 7 被替換了。`,"D to C improves too, from 9 to 6. That route goes D, A, B, C: it uses the stopover at A found a moment ago.":`D 到 C 也改進了，從 9 變成 6。這條路線是 D、A、B、C：它用到了剛才找到的經 A 中轉。`,"3 + 1 beats 7":`3 + 1 勝過 7`,"And a third":`再來第三個`,"Allow C. A to C is 4 and C to D is 2, so A can reach D at last, for 6. B reaches D for 1 + 2 = 3.":`允許 C。A 到 C 是 4，C 到 D 是 2，所以 A 終於能到達 D 了，花費 6。B 到 D 花費 1 + 2 = 3。`,"Each round only ever asks one question of each pair: is it better to go through the new town?":`每一輪對每一對只問一個問題：經過新的城鎮會更好嗎？`,"The last town fills the table":`最後一個城鎮填滿了表`,"Allow D, the town with the road back to A. B to D is 3 and D to A is 2: B to A is 5. C gets to A for 4, and to B for 7.":`允許 D，也就是有路回到 A 的那個城鎮。B 到 D 是 3，D 到 A 是 2：B 到 A 是 5。C 到 A 花 4，到 B 花 7。`,"Every town may now be a stopover, so every entry is a true shortest distance.":`現在每個城鎮都可以作為中轉站，所以每一項都是真正的最短距離。`,"Three loops":`三重迴圈`,"That is the whole algorithm: for each stopover, for each start, for each end, one comparison. It is dynamic programming, and the table after round k holds the best routes that use only the first k towns in between.":`這就是整個演算法：對每個中轉站、每個起點、每個終點，比較一次。這是動態規劃，第 k 輪之後，表裡存的是中間只經過前 k 個城鎮的最佳路線。`,"Negative roads are fine, as long as no loop has a negative total.":`負權的路也沒問題，只要沒有總和為負的環。`,"O(V³) time, O(V²) memory. Good up to a few hundred nodes; beyond that, run Dijkstra from each one.":`O(V³) 時間，O(V²) 記憶體。幾百個節點以內很好用；超過的話，就從每個節點各跑一次 Dijkstra。`},"union-find":{"while x has a parent:":`當 x 有父節點:`,"x ← its parent":`x ← 它的父節點`,"return x                 // the root names the group":`返回 x                 // 根就是組的名字`,"if a ≠ b: make a the parent of b":`如果 a ≠ b: 讓 a 成為 b 的父節點`,"find, with path compression(x):":`帶路徑壓縮的 find(x):`,"point everything on the way straight at root":`讓路上的一切都直接指向 root`,"return root":`返回 root`,"Who is with whom":`誰和誰在一起`,"Are these two connected?":`這兩個連通嗎？`,"Connections arrive one at a time: A with B, C with D… At any moment you may be asked whether two items are connected, directly or through others.":`連線一個一個地到來：A 和 B，C 和 D……任何時候你都可能被問到兩個項是否連通，不管是直接的還是透過別的項。`,"Searching the graph for every question is too slow. <strong>Union-find</strong> keeps track of the groups themselves. To begin with, every item is a group of one.":`每個問題都去搜尋一遍圖太慢了。<strong>並查集</strong>直接記錄這些組本身。一開始，每個項都是隻有自己的一組。`,"Each item is its own group.":`每個項各自一組。`,Union:`合併`,"To join two groups, point one item at the other. B now points at A; D at C; F at E.":`要合併兩個組，就讓一個項指向另一個。現在 B 指向 A；D 指向 C；F 指向 E。`,"An item that points at nothing is a <strong>root</strong>, and the root is the name of its group. Three roots, so three groups.":`不指向任何東西的項是<strong>根</strong>，根就是它所在組的名字。三個根，所以有三個組。`,Find:`查詢`,"Which group is D in? Follow its arrow until there are no more: D leads to C, and C is a root. D’s group is C.":`D 在哪個組？沿著它的箭頭走，直到沒有箭頭為止：D 通向 C，而 C 是根。D 的組是 C。`,"B’s arrow leads to A. Different roots, so B and D are <strong>not</strong> connected. That is the whole test.":`B 的箭頭通向 A。根不同，所以 B 和 D <strong>不</strong>連通。整個檢查就是這樣。`,"D is in group C":`D 在組 C 中`,"Join two groups":`合併兩個組`,"Now connect B and D. Find both roots, A and C, and point one at the other.":`現在連線 B 和 D。找到兩者的根 A 和 C，讓一個指向另一個。`,"One arrow moved four items into the same group. Nobody was relabelled: B and D never pointed at each other, and they are connected all the same.":`移動一個箭頭，就把四個項放進了同一個組。沒有誰被重新標記：B 和 D 從沒互相指向過，但它們照樣連通了。`,"The chains grow":`鏈在變長`,"Ask about D again. Its path to the root is now two arrows long: D, C, A.":`再問一次 D。它到根的路徑現在有兩個箭頭長：D、C、A。`,"Every union can make some paths longer. Left alone, a group can become one long chain, and find slows to a walk.":`每次合併都可能讓某些路徑變長。放任不管的話，一個組可能變成一條長鏈，查詢就慢得像在步行。`,"D is in group A":`D 在組 A 中`,"Path compression":`路徑壓縮`,"Speed-up":`提速`,"The fix costs almost nothing. Having walked from D to the root, point D <em>straight at it</em>. Next time, D is one step from the answer.":`修復幾乎不花什麼代價。從 D 走到根之後，讓 D <em>直接指向它</em>。下次 D 離答案只有一步。`,"Each find flattens the path it used, so the trees stay shallow by themselves.":`每次查詢都會把它走過的路徑壓平，所以樹會自己保持很淺。`,"With this and one more small trick, find and union are as good as O(1) each.":`有了這個再加一個小技巧，查詢和合並每次都幾乎等於 O(1)。`,"one step from its root":`離它的根只有一步`,"Used for networks, clustering, and building spanning trees.":`用於網路、聚類，以及構建生成樹。`},"minimum-spanning-trees":{"sort the edges, cheapest first":`把邊排序，最便宜的在前`,"for each edge, in that order:":`對每個 邊，按那個順序:`,"if its two ends are not yet connected:":`如果 它的兩端還沒有連通:`,"keep the edge          // union":`保留這條邊          // 合併`,"// otherwise it would close a loop: skip it":`// 否則它會形成環：跳過`,"stop when every node is connected":`當每個節點都連通時停止`,"Kruskal’s algorithm":`Kruskal 演算法`,"Connect everything, cheaply":`便宜地連起一切`,"Five towns need joining to one network. Cable can be laid along any road, at the cost shown. Which roads should be used so that every town is connected and the total is as small as possible?":`五個城鎮需要連成一個網路。電纜可以沿任何一條路鋪設，代價如圖所示。應該用哪些路，才能讓每個城鎮都連通，並且總代價儘可能小？`,"The answer never contains a loop, since a loop always has one cable too many. So it is a tree that reaches every node: a <strong>minimum spanning tree</strong>.":`答案裡永遠不會有環，因為環總是多了一根電纜。所以它是一棵到達每個節點的樹：<strong>最小生成樹</strong>。`,"Edges, cheapest first":`邊，最便宜的在前`,"Cable laid":`已鋪電纜`,"Cheapest edge first":`最便宜的邊優先`,"Sort the roads by cost and take them in order. The two cheapest cost 1 each: A to C, and D to E. Neither closes a loop, so both are kept.":`把路按代價排序，按順序取。最便宜的兩條各花 1：A 到 C，D 到 E。兩條都不形成環，所以都保留。`,"There are now two separate groups, and B on its own.":`現在有兩個分開的組，B 單獨一個。`,"Keep taking the cheapest":`繼續取最便宜的`,"Next is C to B, at 2. B was not connected to anything, so the edge is kept. Then B to D, at 3: its ends are in different groups, so it joins them.":`下一條是 C 到 B，花 2。B 還沒和任何東西連通，所以保留這條邊。然後是 B 到 D，花 3：它的兩端在不同的組裡，所以它把兩組連了起來。`,"Every town can now reach every other.":`現在每個城鎮都能到達其他每個城鎮了。`,"Skip anything that closes a loop":`跳過任何會形成環的邊`,"A to B costs 4, but A and B are already connected through C. Adding it would only make a loop. Skip it. The same goes for C to E.":`A 到 B 花 4，但 A 和 B 已經透過 C 連通了。加上它只會形成一個環。跳過。C 到 E 也一樣。`,"“Are these two already connected?” is exactly what union-find answers, which is why the two are used together.":`「這兩個已經連通了嗎？」正是並查集回答的問題，所以兩者總是一起用。`,"A–B would close a loop":`A–B 會形成環`,"The cheapest network":`最便宜的網路`,"Four edges join five towns, for a total of 7. No other choice of roads connects everything for less.":`四條邊連起了五個城鎮，總計 7。沒有其他選路的方法能以更低的代價連起一切。`,"Always taking the cheapest safe edge is a <strong>greedy</strong> method, and here greed is provably right.":`總是取最便宜的安全邊，這是一種<strong>貪婪</strong>方法，而在這裡，貪婪被證明是對的。`,"O(E log E), nearly all of it the sorting.":`O(E log E)，幾乎全花在排序上。`,"n towns always need n − 1 cables.":`n 個城鎮總是需要 n − 1 根電纜。`},"prims-algorithm":{"while some node is outside the tree:":`當 還有節點在樹外:`,"pick the cheapest edge that joins":`選出最便宜的、連線`,"a node inside to a node outside":`樹內節點和樹外節點的邊`,"add that edge, and its outside node,":`把這條邊和它的樹外節點`,"to the tree":`加進樹裡`,"The tree":`樹`,"Grow one tree":`長一棵樹`,"Kruskal built the spanning tree out of the cheapest edges wherever they were, and let the pieces join up. <strong>Prim’s algorithm</strong> reaches the same tree another way: start from one node and grow outward.":`Kruskal 用最便宜的邊構建生成樹，不管它們在哪裡，再讓各部分連起來。<strong>Prim 演算法</strong>用另一種方法得到同樣的樹：從一個節點開始，向外生長。`,"At every step the tree is a single connected piece. The only question is which edge to grow along next.":`每一步樹都是一個連通的整體。唯一的問題是接下來沿著哪條邊生長。`,"start anywhere":`從任何地方開始`,"In the tree":`在樹中`,"Edges kept":`已保留的邊`,"Cost so far":`目前的代價`,"The cheapest edge leaving the tree":`離開樹的最便宜的邊`,"Two roads leave A: 4 to B, 1 to C. Take the cheaper, and C joins the tree.":`從 A 出去有兩條路：到 B 花 4，到 C 花 1。取更便宜的，C 加入樹。`,"The number over each outside node is the cheapest road linking it to the tree so far. B has just improved: 2 through C beats 4 from A. D cannot be reached yet.":`每個樹外節點上方的數字，是目前把它連到樹上的最便宜的路。B 剛剛改進了：經 C 的 2 勝過從 A 出發的 4。D 還到不了。`,"Again, from the whole tree":`再來，從整棵樹出發`,"The cheapest way out of the tree is now the 2 to B. Take it.":`現在離開樹最便宜的路是到 B 的 2。取它。`,"A–B is left with both ends inside, so it can never be used: it would only close a loop. Through B, D comes within reach at 3.":`A–B 的兩端都在樹裡了，所以它永遠用不上：它只會形成環。經過 B，D 可以用 3 到達了。`,"A better offer turns up":`出現了更好的報價`,"D is nearer than E: 3 against 7. D joins.":`D 比 E 近：3 對 7。D 加入。`,"And D has a road to E that costs only 1. E’s number drops from 7 to 1.":`而且 D 有一條到 E 的路只花 1。E 的數字從 7 降到 1。`,"Everyone is in":`全都進來了`,"E joins by the 1. No node is left outside, so the tree is finished: four edges, total cost 7.":`E 透過 1 加入。沒有節點留在樹外了，所以樹完成了：四條邊，總代價 7。`,"It is exactly the tree Kruskal found. Both methods are guaranteed a cheapest tree. Where several trees tie they may pick different ones, but the total always comes out the same.":`這正是 Kruskal 找到的那棵樹。兩種方法都保證得到一棵最便宜的樹。當幾棵樹代價相同時，它們可能選出不同的樹，但總代價總是一樣的。`,"Dijkstra’s cousin":`Dijkstra 的近親`,"Keep the outside nodes in a min-heap, ordered by their number, and each step is a pop followed by a few updates.":`把樹外節點按它們的數字放進一個最小堆積，每一步就是一次彈出，再加幾次更新。`,"That is Dijkstra’s algorithm with one change. Dijkstra’s number is the distance from the <em>start</em>. Prim’s is the distance from the <em>tree</em>.":`這就是隻改了一處的 Dijkstra 演算法。Dijkstra 的數字是離<em>起點</em>的距離。Prim 的是離<em>樹</em>的距離。`,"O(E log V) with a heap, the same as Kruskal. Prim needs no sorting and no union-find.":`用堆積是 O(E log V)，和 Kruskal 一樣。Prim 不需要排序，也不需要並查集。`}};export{n as default,e as resizing,t as tries};